Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:05.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(1917,150)}听译、时间轴：刘巍然（学酥）
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.33,0:00:12.76,Default,,0,0,0,,大家好 欢迎来到CME 296：扩散与大型视觉模型\NHello, everyone, and welcome to CME 296, Diffusion & Large Vision Models.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.76,0:00:14.59,Default,,0,0,0,,我叫Afshine\NMy name is Afshine,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.59,0:00:19.36,Default,,0,0,0,,我将和坐在后面的Shervine一起教这门课\Nand I'm going to be teaching this class with Shervine, who's in the back.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.36,0:00:24.08,Default,,0,0,0,,在正式开始课程之前 我先介绍一下我们自己\NSo, before we start, I'm just going to introduce ourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.08,0:00:30.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Shervine和我是双胞胎兄弟 我们有非常相似的背景\NSo, Shervine and I are twin brothers, and we have very similar backgrounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.15,0:00:35.41,Default,,0,0,0,,我们都在法国一所叫巴黎中央理工的学校读的本科\NSo, we both went to a school in France called Centrale Paris.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.41,0:00:38.69,Default,,0,0,0,,之后 我们来到美国读研究生\NAnd then, we came here to the U.S. to do grad school.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.69,0:00:41.55,Default,,0,0,0,,我自己去了MIT\NSo, on my end, I went to MIT.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.55,0:00:43.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Shervine则去了\NAnd then, Shervine went to
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.07,0:00:44.92,Default,,0,0,0,,ICME（计算与数学工程研究所）\Nthe ICME (Institute for Computational & Mathematical Engineering),
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.92,0:00:46.71,Default,,0,0,0,,这是斯坦福大学的一个研究院\NDepartment at Stanford.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.32,0:00:52.39,Default,,0,0,0,,我们之后在工业界的经历也非常相似\NAnd then, after that, we've had pretty similar backgrounds in the industry.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.39,0:00:55.13,Default,,0,0,0,,我们都先去了Uber\NSo, we both went to Uber first.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.13,0:00:57.28,Default,,0,0,0,,然后去了Google\NAnd then, we went to Google.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.28,0:00:59.45,Default,,0,0,0,,现在 我们都在Netflix\NAnd now, we're both at Netflix.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.56,0:01:05.65,Default,,0,0,0,,我们对能来教这门课感到非常兴奋\NAnd the reason why we're so excited to be teaching this class
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.65,0:01:12.04,Default,,0,0,0,,因为回想10年前 在我们刚入行的时候\Nis because back in the day, 10 years ago, when we started in the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.04,0:01:16.41,Default,,0,0,0,,我们的第一个项目其实就是一个计算机视觉项目\Nwe actually had our first project, be a computer vision project.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.57,0:01:22.99,Default,,0,0,0,,这个领域的进步速度简直令人难以置信\NAnd it's been crazy the amount of progress that we've seen in the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.99,0:01:28.21,Default,,0,0,0,,这是当时我们能生成的图像\NSo, this is the kind of images that we were able to generate.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.21,0:01:30.71,Default,,0,0,0,,那是在2014年\NSo, it's back in 2014.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.71,0:01:37.27,Default,,0,0,0,,当时主要能生成的就是低分辨率的黑白图片\NSo, it was mostly low-resolution black-and-white pictures.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.55,0:01:42.03,Default,,0,0,0,,例如 这里给出了一些生成的数字或人脸图片\NSo, for instance, here, there're some digits or human faces.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.03,0:01:43.73,Default,,0,0,0,,而大家都知道\NAnd as you all know,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.73,0:01:50.77,Default,,0,0,0,,如今 我们已经能生成高分辨率的彩色图像了\Nnowadays, we're able to generate high-resolution colored images,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.77,0:01:54.79,Default,,0,0,0,,例如 这两张图像就是我用ChatGPT生成的\Nso, for instance, those ones that I generated with ChatGPT.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.67,0:02:00.25,Default,,0,0,0,,这门课的目标就是\NAnd the goal of this class is to understand
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.25,0:02:05.67,Default,,0,0,0,,理解这些图像生成模型是如何工作的 以及为什么生成效果这么好\Nhow this image generation models work, and what makes them work so well.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.16,0:02:13.29,Default,,0,0,0,,具体来说 这门课有两个主要目标\NSo, in particular, this class has two main goals.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.29,0:02:14.51,Default,,0,0,0,,第一个目标是\NSo, the first goal is
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.51,0:02:20.97,Default,,0,0,0,,理解图像生成背后的范式是什么\Nto understand the paradigms behind how we can generate these images.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.97,0:02:22.19,Default,,0,0,0,,第二个目标是\NAnd the second one is
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.19,0:02:27.37,Default,,0,0,0,,理解底层模型是如何训练和评估的\Nto understand how the underlying models are trained and evaluated.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.48,0:02:35.44,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你现在在这个教室里 还在犹豫这门课是否适合你\NSo, in case you're here in this room, and still wondering if this class is good for you,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.44,0:02:40.99,Default,,0,0,0,,我想说 如果你对以下方面感兴趣 这门课就适合你\NI would say that this class is good if you have, in general, an interest in
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.99,0:02:44.25,Default,,0,0,0,,理解图像生成模型的工作原理\Nunderstanding how image generation models work,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.25,0:02:48.84,Default,,0,0,0,,特别地 如果这是你职业发展方向的一部分\Nand in particular, if this is something that you wanted to do as a career goal,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.84,0:02:54.68,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你想进入研究领域 做这个领域的研究科学家\Nif you want to go in the field of research to do peer research scientists,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.68,0:02:59.51,Default,,0,0,0,,研究如何更好地生成图像\Nto research how to generate images in a better way,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.51,0:03:05.83,Default,,0,0,0,,或者你自己想在业余时间通过做个人项目来探索这个方向\Nor if you are yourself interested to do that on your personal time as a personal project,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.83,0:03:08.68,Default,,0,0,0,,又或者纯粹出于好奇心来这里\Nor just if you're here out of pure curiosity.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.77,0:03:15.15,Default,,0,0,0,,话虽如此 我想给大家一个提醒\NWith that being said, I want to give a warning.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.15,0:03:20.80,Default,,0,0,0,,这门课其实有相当高的先修要求\NSo, this class actually has a pretty strong set of prerequisites.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.80,0:03:22.71,Default,,0,0,0,,我不会回避这一点\NAnd I'm not going to hide it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.71,0:03:25.29,Default,,0,0,0,,这张幻灯片\NSo, this slide is just there
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.29,0:03:29.39,Default,,0,0,0,,列出了我认为需要具备的先修知识\Nto enumerate the kinds of prerequisites that I think are good to have,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.39,0:03:32.35,Default,,0,0,0,,免得你们之后感到意外\Njust so that you're not surprised.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.35,0:03:37.53,Default,,0,0,0,,首先 如果你有一些线性代数的基础\NSo, first of all, in case you have some background in linear algebra,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.53,0:03:40.84,Default,,0,0,0,,例如 你知道什么是向量 什么是矩阵\Nfor instance, if you know what a vector is, what a matrix is,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.84,0:03:49.20,Default,,0,0,0,,知道怎么做线性代数运算 知道什么是梯度 什么是向量场的散度\Nhow you do operations, what is the gradient, what is the divergence of a vector field,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.20,0:03:50.92,Default,,0,0,0,,那就太好了\Nthat would be great.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.92,0:03:55.04,Default,,0,0,0,,如果不是全都知道 也没关系\NIf you don't know everything, that's OK too.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.04,0:03:59.05,Default,,0,0,0,,在这门课中 我们不会假设你什么都知道\NSo, in this class, we will not assume that you know everything,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.05,0:04:03.60,Default,,0,0,0,,但你至少需要有一些基础知识 这非常重要\Nbut if you have at least some foundations, it's quite important to have it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.69,0:04:07.21,Default,,0,0,0,,线性代数是第一门先修课程\NSo, linear algebra is one.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.21,0:04:10.64,Default,,0,0,0,,第二门比较重要的先修课程是概率论\NSecond one that's quite important is probability theory.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.40,0:04:18.96,Default,,0,0,0,,具体来说 你需要知道Bayes规则 知道条件概率和边际概率\NSo, in particular, Bayes' rule, conditional/marginal probabilities,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.96,0:04:22.72,Default,,0,0,0,,知道什么是期望 什么是协方差矩阵\Nwhat is an expectation, what is the covariance matrix,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.72,0:04:25.23,Default,,0,0,0,,以及什么是高斯分布\Nand what is the Gaussian distribution.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.23,0:04:28.36,Default,,0,0,0,,同样 如果不是全都知道 也没关系\NAgain, if you don't know everything, it's fine,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.36,0:04:31.97,Default,,0,0,0,,但至少要知道大部分 或者至少听说过\Nbut at least most of it, or at least if you've heard of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.28,0:04:36.01,Default,,0,0,0,,然后是微分方程\NThen, you have differential equations.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.01,0:04:40.55,Default,,0,0,0,,在这门课中 我们会讲到如何使用ODE和SDE\NSo here, we'll see how we can use ODEs and SDEs,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.55,0:04:45.71,Default,,0,0,0,,也就是常微分方程（ODE）和随机微分方程（SDE）\Nso, Ordinary Differential Equations, and Stochastic Differential Equations,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.71,0:04:48.57,Default,,0,0,0,,我们会介绍这两种方程为什么重要 以及如何求解这两种方程\Nand how they matter, and how we solve them.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.17,0:04:54.64,Default,,0,0,0,,最后同样重要的是 一些机器学习基础\NAnd then, last but not least, there're some basics of ML.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.64,0:05:00.09,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你知道如何使用神经网络来训练模型\NSo, if you know how you train a model, just in general, using a neural network,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.09,0:05:03.88,Default,,0,0,0,,怎么做训练 怎么做推理\Nhow you do training, how you do inference,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.88,0:05:05.32,Default,,0,0,0,,那就太好了\Nthat would be great.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.32,0:05:06.76,Default,,0,0,0,,但话说回来\NBut again,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.76,0:05:12.95,Default,,0,0,0,,我们会以非详尽的、直觉性的方式来复习这些概念\Nwe will try to review these concepts in a non-exhaustive way, in an intuitive way.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.95,0:05:16.01,Default,,0,0,0,,但是 我认为了解这些知识会带来很大的帮助\NBut yeah, just knowing those, I think, would be great.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.41,0:05:19.65,Default,,0,0,0,,这是我给出的第一个提醒\NSo, that's one warning.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.65,0:05:26.36,Default,,0,0,0,,我要说的第二点是 这个领域从整体上看技术性非常强\NThe second thing that I will say is that this field is very technical in general.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.36,0:05:31.27,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你读一篇计算机视觉图像生成的论文\NSo, if you read a computer vision image generation paper,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.27,0:05:34.81,Default,,0,0,0,,你会看到到处都是公式\Nyou will see that there are formulas all over the place.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.81,0:05:39.04,Default,,0,0,0,,这门课的目标不是深入所有细节\NSo, the goal of this class will not be to go into all of these details.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.04,0:05:44.88,Default,,0,0,0,,我们会努力在不回避数学的同时\NSo, we will try to strike a balance between not shying away from the math,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.88,0:05:48.72,Default,,0,0,0,,帮助你了解哪些是重要的公式\Njust understanding what are the important formulas,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.72,0:05:53.41,Default,,0,0,0,,同时也要帮助你了解为什么会有这些公式\Nbut also at the same time, just understand why they're there.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.83,0:05:58.33,Default,,0,0,0,,我们会非常强调直觉\NSo, we'll try to make a big emphasis on intuition.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.29,0:06:02.83,Default,,0,0,0,,到目前为止都清楚吗？\NAll good so far?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.29,0:06:05.55,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NOK, great.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.55,0:06:08.07,Default,,0,0,0,,接下来说一下课程安排\NSo, just moving on to some logistics.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.07,0:06:15.61,Default,,0,0,0,,我们每周五下午3:30到5:20在这个教室上课\NSo, we'll have this class every Friday from 3:30pm to 5:20pm in this class.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.61,0:06:20.20,Default,,0,0,0,,再补充一些课程安排的信息 这是一门2学分的课\NAnd just again logistics, so it's a 2-unit class.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.20,0:06:25.71,Default,,0,0,0,,你可以选择按字母等级（A/B/C/D）计分 或者只记通过与不通过\NYou can take it either as a letter, or credit/non-credit.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.73,0:06:30.44,Default,,0,0,0,,如你们所见 现场布置了录制设备 所以课程会被录像\NSo, as you can see with the setup, the lectures are recorded.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.44,0:06:34.13,Default,,0,0,0,,课程视频会尽量在周六晚上之前发布\NWe'll try to post the videos by Saturday evening.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.13,0:06:39.31,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你希望远程观看课程视频 那不来现场上课也没关系\NSo, for you watching remotely, if you don't come to class, it's all good.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.31,0:06:45.35,Default,,0,0,0,,课程视频会在录制后的一天之内发布\NWe'll be just publishing the videos within a day of it happening.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.35,0:06:47.36,Default,,0,0,0,,关于考试\NAnd then, in terms of the exams,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.76,0:06:50.83,Default,,0,0,0,,这门课没有作业\Nthis class has no homework,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.93,0:06:54.79,Default,,0,0,0,,但我们有两次考试\Nbut we have two exams.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.79,0:06:59.00,Default,,0,0,0,,一次是期中考试 一次是期末考试\NOne is the midterm, and the other one is the final.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.00,0:07:03.36,Default,,0,0,0,,这门课的考试形式 你可能喜欢也可能不喜欢\NAnd here, the kind of exam that you may or may not like,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.36,0:07:06.91,Default,,0,0,0,,这门课是纸笔考试\Nbut it is a pen-and-paper kind of exam,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.91,0:07:13.24,Default,,0,0,0,,我们在课上讲的概念\Nmeaning the lectures that we will do will be about concepts
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.24,0:07:17.00,Default,,0,0,0,,都会出现在考试中\Nthat will be covered in the exam.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.00,0:07:23.83,Default,,0,0,0,,重要的不是记住所有细节\NAnd the important thing is to not know all the details, again,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.83,0:07:32.00,Default,,0,0,0,,只需掌握主要公式 以及理解它们为什么存在\Njust the general formulas and mainly the intuition as to why they're there.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.00,0:07:39.92,Default,,0,0,0,,如果考试风格对你来说有点模糊 我们有一门类似的LLM课程\NSo, in case it's a little bit vague for you, we have a similar class that we do for LLMs.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.92,0:07:42.56,Default,,0,0,0,,不知道你们有没有听说过CME 295\NI'm not sure if you've heard CME 295.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.56,0:07:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,这两门课程的考试形式很类似\NSo, the format of the exams is very similar.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.91,0:07:48.60,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你对考试形式感兴趣\NSo, in case you're interested,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.60,0:07:55.21,Default,,0,0,0,,我们放了一个链接 里面有那门课程的考试内容\Nwe put just a link to one kind of exam that you can expect.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.40,0:07:59.97,Default,,0,0,0,,当然 题目不会完全一样 因为两门课程的主题不相同\NOf course, it will not be the same questions, because it's also different topics,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.97,0:08:01.99,Default,,0,0,0,,但能让你对考试形式有个大致的了解\Nbut it will give you a good idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.03,0:08:07.08,Default,,0,0,0,,关于考试 还有什么问题吗？\NAny questions on the exams?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.80,0:08:12.13,Default,,0,0,0,,都很清楚了？\NSuper clear?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.80,0:08:16.03,Default,,0,0,0,,我知道这才第1节课 我就在讲考试了\NYeah, I know it's the first lecture, and I'm talking about exams already.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.03,0:08:19.80,Default,,0,0,0,,别担心 距离期中考试还有四周时间 我们有的是时间准备\NSo, yeah, don't worry. It's four weeks away and we have time.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.83,0:08:23.47,Default,,0,0,0,,这门课会很有趣的 我保证\NAnd yeah, it's a fun class, I promise.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.95,0:08:25.77,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NCool.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.96,0:08:31.15,Default,,0,0,0,,关于课程资料 我们有一个课程网站\NIn terms of the material, we have a class website.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.64,0:08:37.88,Default,,0,0,0,,我们会在网站上发布课程幻灯片和录像\NAnd on that website, we'll be publishing the slides and the recordings as well,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.88,0:08:44.73,Default,,0,0,0,,这样你就可以提前拿到幻灯片做批注了\Nso, just so that you have a way to get the slides in advance for annotation purposes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.73,0:08:49.96,Default,,0,0,0,,我们会在每节课的前一天发布幻灯片\NOne thing we will do is to publish the slides the day before the lecture,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.96,0:08:51.64,Default,,0,0,0,,也就是在周四晚上发布\Nso, Thursday evening.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.52,0:08:55.57,Default,,0,0,0,,你可以下载幻灯片 自己做批注\NSo, you can get the slides and make some annotations.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.77,0:09:02.60,Default,,0,0,0,,请注意 网页右上角还有一个写着“速查表”的标签\NAnd if you saw, there is a tab also, top right, CHEATSHEET.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.60,0:09:10.16,Default,,0,0,0,,我们还发布了一份关于本课程内容的4页浓缩版速查表\NWe also published a condensed 4-page cheat sheet on the content of this class.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.16,0:09:17.01,Default,,0,0,0,,速查表汇集了所有主要的公式和概念\NSo, it gathers all the main formulas and concepts.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.48,0:09:23.28,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你今天就去查阅速查表 会发现有些部分还看不懂\NSo, our goal is, if you look at it today, if you don't understand parts of it,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.28,0:09:28.99,Default,,0,0,0,,我们的目标是 在课程结束时 让你们能看懂速查表上的所有内容\Nour goal is, by the end of this class, to have everything be very clear.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.00,0:09:32.00,Default,,0,0,0,,如果能做到这一点 我觉得就很棒了\NSo, if we achieve that goal, I think that's great.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.89,0:09:34.65,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NCool.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.20,0:09:36.95,Default,,0,0,0,,最后再说一点\NOK, so, last thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.95,0:09:41.11,Default,,0,0,0,,课程通知会发布在Canvas上\NSo, for any announcements, we'll be posting them on Canvas.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.11,0:09:45.93,Default,,0,0,0,,我们在Ed论坛上还开放了本课程的讨论专栏\NAnd then, we have a forum for class discussions on Ed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.37,0:09:49.59,Default,,0,0,0,,当然 也欢迎随时联系我们\NAnd of course, feel free to reach out to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.59,0:09:54.36,Default,,0,0,0,,幻灯片上有联系方式 有任何问题都可以找我们\NSo, there are the addresses here on the slides, if you need anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.60,0:09:57.21,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NCool.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.21,0:09:59.83,Default,,0,0,0,,课程安排就这些信息了\NI think these are all the logistics.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.99,0:10:05.59,Default,,0,0,0,,关于课程安排 大家还有什么问题吗？\NAre there any questions so far on just how the class works?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.45,0:10:11.32,Default,,0,0,0,,请问\NYeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.13,0:10:14.23,Default,,0,0,0,,他的问题是...\NSo, the question...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.23,0:10:17.91,Default,,0,0,0,,我也给远程听课的同学重复一下提问\NSo, I'm going to also repeat the question for people at home.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.91,0:10:20.05,Default,,0,0,0,,期中和期末分别考多久？\NSo, how long is the midterm and the exam?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.05,0:10:21.72,Default,,0,0,0,,都是1小时30分钟\NIt's 1 hour and 30 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.80,0:10:26.67,Default,,0,0,0,,好的 太好了 我觉得大家应该没有其他问题了\NOK, cool. I think we're all good then.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.69,0:10:28.36,Default,,0,0,0,,太好了\NGreat.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.36,0:10:29.73,Default,,0,0,0,,让我们开始吧\NSo, let's get started.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.73,0:10:36.44,Default,,0,0,0,,我想指出的是 在这门课的幻灯片中\NSo, I just want to call out that in the slides of this class,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.44,0:10:41.47,Default,,0,0,0,,我们会主要讲解概念\Nwhat we will do is to explain the concepts in the main part,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.47,0:10:46.71,Default,,0,0,0,,但我们会始终放上参考论文的链接\Nbut we will always put a reference to the paper
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.71,0:10:50.33,Default,,0,0,0,,论文中会更深入地讨论我们所讲的内容\Nthat talks more in depth about what we're talking about,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.33,0:10:54.21,Default,,0,0,0,,因为我们只有大约8节课 每节2小时\Njust because we only have, I believe, 8 lectures of 2 hours,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.21,0:10:57.91,Default,,0,0,0,,所以我们远远无法涵盖所有细节\Nso, we have nowhere near covering everything in detail.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.91,0:10:59.80,Default,,0,0,0,,有兴趣的话可以去看看相应的论文\NSo, yeah, feel free to look at them.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.80,0:11:05.37,Default,,0,0,0,,考试不要求掌握论文内容 只是给你们参考\NThey will not be required to know for the exam, it's just for your own reference.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.11,0:11:08.80,Default,,0,0,0,,有一个重要说明\NOK, an important note.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.76,0:11:11.08,Default,,0,0,0,,我前面提到\NSo, I mentioned that
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.08,0:11:18.60,Default,,0,0,0,,这个领域的论文在技术性和数学公式方面非常复杂\Nthe papers in the field are crazy in terms of technicality and math formulas,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.60,0:11:21.72,Default,,0,0,0,,符号约定方面也是如此\Nthe same goes for conventions.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.72,0:11:27.13,Default,,0,0,0,,你会发现 不同的论文之间符号的写法都不一样\NSo, you will see that from paper to paper, things are noted differently,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.13,0:11:29.83,Default,,0,0,0,,这会令人感到非常困惑\Nand it can be very confusing.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.83,0:11:33.31,Default,,0,0,0,,比如 你会看到有一个时间t\NSo, for instance, you will see there is a time t
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.31,0:11:35.39,Default,,0,0,0,,有时候t在0和1之间\Nthat sometimes is between 0 and 1,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.39,0:11:37.48,Default,,0,0,0,,有时候t在0和T之间\Nsometimes it's between 0 and T,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.48,0:11:39.79,Default,,0,0,0,,有时候是反过来的\Nsometimes it's in reverse,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.79,0:11:46.95,Default,,0,0,0,,有时候ε被写成z或x_0或x_1等等\Nsometimes ε is z or x_0 or x_1, etc.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.95,0:11:52.04,Default,,0,0,0,,所以 在这门课中 我们会做三件事\NSo, in this class, what we will try to do is three things.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.08,0:11:58.47,Default,,0,0,0,,第一 我们会尽量使用最常见的符号\NFirst is, we will always try to rely on the most commonly used notations,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.47,0:12:02.04,Default,,0,0,0,,这样当你去查阅那些论文时 就不会迷失方向\Nso that when you go and refer to those papers, you're not lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.49,0:12:08.71,Default,,0,0,0,,第二 我们会尽可能保持符号的一致性\NThe second one is, we will try to stay consistent as much as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.71,0:12:14.95,Default,,0,0,0,,如果我们选定了一个符号 就会坚持使用这个符号 让你不会感到困惑\NSo, if we take a notation, we'll try to keep it so that you're not confused.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.95,0:12:20.19,Default,,0,0,0,,第三 如果我们修改了符号 那我们会明确指出来\NAnd if we don't keep it, we'll just make sure to call it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.11,0:12:26.23,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NOK, great.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.23,0:12:28.11,Default,,0,0,0,,正如我所说\NSo, as I mentioned,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.11,0:12:34.45,Default,,0,0,0,,这门课的核心是理解图像生成模型是如何工作的\Nthis class is all about understanding how image generation models work.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.45,0:12:37.47,Default,,0,0,0,,幻灯片里给出的是一个典型的图像生成流程\NSo here, you have a typical setup
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.47,0:12:43.97,Default,,0,0,0,,你有一个提示词 用来指定你想生成什么图像\Nwhere you have, let's say, a prompt, where you specify what you want to generate.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.97,0:12:46.95,Default,,0,0,0,,这里 我想要生成的图像是“一只正在阅读一本书的泰迪熊”\NSo here, I want to generate “a teddy bear reading a book”.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.95,0:12:49.24,Default,,0,0,0,,我把提示词输入给某个模型\NAnd I put that in some model.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.24,0:12:52.95,Default,,0,0,0,,模型会生成一张图像\NAnd then, the model generates an image.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.95,0:12:55.44,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是我们这门课程所要讲的内容\NSo, this is what we want to cover.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.67,0:13:04.11,Default,,0,0,0,,看似很简单 实际很复杂\NBut as easy as it seems, it's actually quite complex.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.11,0:13:07.37,Default,,0,0,0,,图像生成过程所涉及的环节非常多\NThere're a lot of things moving pieces everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.37,0:13:10.59,Default,,0,0,0,,接下来 我会指出我们这门课程要涵盖的主要环节\NAnd I'm going to call out the main moving pieces that we'll cover.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.41,0:13:18.51,Default,,0,0,0,,第一个环节是 假定你拥有某个模型\NSo, the first one is, if you suppose that you have some model,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.51,0:13:22.11,Default,,0,0,0,,你是如何用这个模型来生成图像的？\Nhow do you go about generating images?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.11,0:13:24.93,Default,,0,0,0,,生成图像的过程是什么？\NWhat is the process of generating images?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.29,0:13:29.01,Default,,0,0,0,,在文本世界里 生成过程相当简单\NSo, in the text world, it is quite easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.01,0:13:34.21,Default,,0,0,0,,最常见的范式是一次生成一个词元\NThe most common paradigm is you generate one token at a time,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.21,0:13:39.37,Default,,0,0,0,,因为人在说话和写字时都是按顺序一次写出一个词 这很直观\Nbecause that's also what people talk and how people write, so it's quite intuitive.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.37,0:13:42.48,Default,,0,0,0,,但在图像世界里 生成过程就不那么直接了\NBut in the image world, it's not straightforward.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.68,0:13:50.84,Default,,0,0,0,,我们将在第1、第2、第3节课重点讨论这部分内容\NSo, we will focus Lectures 1, 2, and 3 on this part.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.84,0:13:54.28,Default,,0,0,0,,我们将介绍目前最主流的几种方法\NAnd we will cover the main ways of doing it,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.28,0:13:56.24,Default,,0,0,0,,它们也是当今最常用的方法\Nwhich are the most commonly used today,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.24,0:14:02.25,Default,,0,0,0,,分别是扩散、分数匹配、流匹配\Nwhich are diffusion, score matching, and flow matching.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.81,0:14:07.44,Default,,0,0,0,,随后 我们会介绍\NThen, we will look at
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.44,0:14:13.68,Default,,0,0,0,,如何给模型设定条件 让模型根据给定的条件来生成图像\Nhow we can condition our model to generate these images to start with.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.68,0:14:16.77,Default,,0,0,0,,我们将在第4节课介绍这部分内容\NSo, we'll cover that in Lecture 4.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.77,0:14:22.08,Default,,0,0,0,,某种意义上说 我们想要引导模型生成某些东西\NSo, in some sense we want to guide the model to generate something,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.08,0:14:23.69,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是我们在第4节课要讨论的内容\Nand this is what we will cover.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.69,0:14:24.45,Default,,0,0,0,,我们也会讲到\NWe'll also cover
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.45,0:14:30.23,Default,,0,0,0,,如何在一个所谓“合理”的空间中表示图像\Nhow to represent images in a space that “quote unquote” makes sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.51,0:14:38.39,Default,,0,0,0,,第5节课将介绍模型架构\NSo, Lecture 5 is going to be about the model architecture.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.25,0:14:44.95,Default,,0,0,0,,我们将介绍当前最常用的骨干网络\NSo, we'll take a look at the backbones that are most commonly used today.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.95,0:14:50.52,Default,,0,0,0,,以前 你可能听说过U-Net\NSo, back in the day, you may have heard of U-Net as being something that was used.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.52,0:14:53.40,Default,,0,0,0,,但目前 图像生成的模型架构\NBut there's currently a convergence of architectures
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.40,0:14:56.76,Default,,0,0,0,,正在向基于Transformer的架构收敛\Nmore towards Transformer-based architectures,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.76,0:14:59.57,Default,,0,0,0,,例如扩散Transformer\Nsuch as the diffusion Transformer,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.57,0:15:03.12,Default,,0,0,0,,以及多模态扩散Transformer等变体\Nand variants such as the multi-modal diffusion Transformer.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.12,0:15:05.31,Default,,0,0,0,,我们将在第5节课介绍这部分内容\NAnd we will take a look at those there.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.76,0:15:13.47,Default,,0,0,0,,第6节课将介绍如何训练这些模型\NThen, Lecture 6 will be around knowing how to train those models.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.47,0:15:20.96,Default,,0,0,0,,具体来说 如何让模型学习生成图像\NSo, in particular, how do you have your model understand how to generate images,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.96,0:15:25.77,Default,,0,0,0,,你可能还需要使用后训练方法\Nand any post-training approaches that you may also need.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.77,0:15:31.83,Default,,0,0,0,,还有一个在工业界特别重要的话题\NThere's also something that is quite important, especially in the industry, which is
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.83,0:15:36.27,Default,,0,0,0,,你有了你的模型 但你想让它跑得更快\Nyou have your model, but you want to run it quicker,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.27,0:15:39.08,Default,,0,0,0,,因为你的实际部署环境有一些限制\Nbecause you have some constraints in your setup.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.08,0:15:42.49,Default,,0,0,0,,因此 我们还会介绍蒸馏技术\NSo, we will see also distillation techniques.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.49,0:15:44.61,Default,,0,0,0,,这些就是第6节课的内容\NSo, this will be in Lecture 6.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.61,0:15:51.08,Default,,0,0,0,,最后 第7节课的内容是生成图像的质量评估\NAnd finally, Lecture 7 will be about evaluating images,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.08,0:15:54.55,Default,,0,0,0,,因为如果你看一张图像...\Nbecause if you look at an image...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.55,0:15:55.39,Default,,0,0,0,,不知道你们怎么看这个问题\NI'm not sure about you,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.39,0:16:02.87,Default,,0,0,0,,但定义一张图像好不好 方法其实并不那么显然\Nbut it's not super obvious how you would define an image as being great or not great.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.03,0:16:09.19,Default,,0,0,0,,你会发现这个领域在评估指标方面充满了各种缩写\NSo, you will see that the field is full of acronyms when it comes to metrics.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.19,0:16:15.12,Default,,0,0,0,,每一个缩写背后都有其存在的原因 我们会逐一讲解\NAnd each of those is there actually for a reason, and we'll try to see that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.12,0:16:17.79,Default,,0,0,0,,我们在第7节课会讲到的第二个内容是\NAnd then, the second thing that we will see is
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.79,0:16:25.91,Default,,0,0,0,,现在我们已经有了可以理解图像的多模态大语言模型\Nthis emergence of multi-modal LLMs that also understand images
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.91,0:16:28.47,Default,,0,0,0,,可以用多模态大语言模型来帮助我们评估图像\Nthat can also help us to evaluate them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.85,0:16:31.85,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是第7节课的内容\NSo, this will be for Lecture 7.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.75,0:16:41.25,Default,,0,0,0,,正如我前面所提到的 今天我们将从生成范式1开始\NAnd today, as mentioned, we will start with the generation paradigm 1.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.25,0:16:45.60,Default,,0,0,0,,特别地 我们将介绍扩散模型\NAnd in particular, we will look at diffusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.60,0:16:47.44,Default,,0,0,0,,有多少人听说过扩散模型？\NSo, who has heard of diffusion?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.79,0:16:50.69,Default,,0,0,0,,好的 每个人都听说过\NYeah, OK, so, everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.20,0:16:57.29,Default,,0,0,0,,我们将超越直觉层面的“大概知道它怎么工作”\NSo, we will see beyond the general intuition of roughly how that works.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.29,0:17:00.81,Default,,0,0,0,,我们将精确地介绍如何定义扩散模型\NWe'll see exactly how this was defined,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.81,0:17:06.27,Default,,0,0,0,,以及是什么让这个目标函数在实践中变得可处理\Nand what is making this objective be tractable in practice.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.47,0:17:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,我想指出的一点是\NSo, one thing that I want to call out is
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.00,0:17:18.87,Default,,0,0,0,,在前三节课中 我们会假设没有任何输入条件\Nin the first three lectures, we will assume that there is nothing as input.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.81,0:17:26.09,Default,,0,0,0,,我们有一些作为训练集的数据分布\NSo, we have some distribution of data that we use as training sets.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.09,0:17:30.24,Default,,0,0,0,,我们想做的就是生成跟训练集数据类似的图像\NAnd what we want is to generate images that are like them.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.24,0:17:33.88,Default,,0,0,0,,用数学语言来说 我们想要一个模型\NSo, in mathematical terms, we want to have a model
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.88,0:17:38.53,Default,,0,0,0,,能够依数据分布采样一个观测值\Nthat is able to sample an observation from the data distribution.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.53,0:17:43.89,Default,,0,0,0,,某种意义上说 在包括这一节课在内的前三节课中\NSo, in a sense, we'll only focus on unconditioned generations
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.89,0:17:46.16,Default,,0,0,0,,我们都只关注无条件图像生成模型\Nfor the first three lectures including this one.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.99,0:17:49.89,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NCool.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.89,0:17:52.23,Default,,0,0,0,,说到数据分布\NSo, speaking of data distribution.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.17,0:17:57.37,Default,,0,0,0,,假设我们有一组图像\NSo, let's suppose we have a set of images.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.37,0:18:01.71,Default,,0,0,0,,泰迪熊会是这门课程的一个贯穿始终的例子\NSo, here a long running example will be Teddy Bears.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.71,0:18:05.87,Default,,0,0,0,,假设我们有一批泰迪熊图像作为训练图像\NSo, here let's say we have a collection of Teddy Bears as training images.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.87,0:18:11.55,Default,,0,0,0,,我们的目标是找到一种方法\NOur goal is to understand a way
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.55,0:18:16.47,Default,,0,0,0,,依数据分布采样一个新的观测值\Nto sample an observation from that data distribution that is new.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.47,0:18:18.56,Default,,0,0,0,,所以我们想做的是\NSo, what we want to do is
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.56,0:18:24.45,Default,,0,0,0,,能够生成一张属于该数据分布的图像\Nto be able to generate an image that is in that data distribution.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.45,0:18:26.89,Default,,0,0,0,,例如 这里生成了一只长颈鹿\NSo here, for instance, giraffe.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.09,0:18:33.88,Default,,0,0,0,,再次强调 这里是无条件生成\NAnd again, just emphasizing that this is unconditioned.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.88,0:18:36.83,Default,,0,0,0,,我们没有输入任何条件\NWe're not putting anything as input.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.83,0:18:40.77,Default,,0,0,0,,我们只是想生成一个服从该分布的样本\NWe just want to generate a sample that is following that distribution.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.69,0:18:44.16,Default,,0,0,0,,我们该怎么做呢？\NSo, how do we do this?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.59,0:18:50.35,Default,,0,0,0,,你会发现 目前已有的几乎所有方法\NSo, you will see that most if not all methods out there,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.35,0:18:53.19,Default,,0,0,0,,都有一个共同点\Nthey all have something in common.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.19,0:18:59.16,Default,,0,0,0,,几乎所有方法的图像生成过程都从噪声开始\NThey all start their image generation process from noise.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.16,0:19:04.60,Default,,0,0,0,,从噪声出发 然后逐步精炼图像 直到得到最终的生成结果\NSo, they start from noise, and then, they refine the image to be the final image.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.60,0:19:08.87,Default,,0,0,0,,我想花点时间解释一下为什么是这样\NSo, I want to just spend some time on why that is the case.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.99,0:19:12.85,Default,,0,0,0,,顺便说一下 我们会定义噪声是什么意思\NSo, we'll define what noise means, by the way,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.85,0:19:18.23,Default,,0,0,0,,因为当你看到噪声这个词时 你一般也会看到类似这张灰蒙蒙的图\Nbecause you will see the term noise, and then, you will see this grayish image.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.23,0:19:20.65,Default,,0,0,0,,你会看到\NSo, you will see that
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.65,0:19:26.69,Default,,0,0,0,,这个噪声实际上可以依一个简单的分布采样\Nthis noise is actually something that you can sample from an easy distribution,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.69,0:19:29.48,Default,,0,0,0,,剧透一下 这个简单的分布就是高斯分布\Nthe Gaussian distribution, spoiler alert.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.48,0:19:34.31,Default,,0,0,0,,我们一般会从噪声作为生成起点的第一个原因是\NSo, the first reason why it is something that we want to do is because
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.31,0:19:36.60,Default,,0,0,0,,很容易采样噪声\Nit is easy to sample from noise.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.60,0:19:38.13,Default,,0,0,0,,很容易获得噪声\NIt is easy to have some noise.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.51,0:19:41.75,Default,,0,0,0,,第二个原因是\NThe second thing is,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.75,0:19:49.07,Default,,0,0,0,,噪声具有随机性 让你能生成不同的图像\Nnoise has some randomness that allows you to generate different images.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.07,0:19:52.52,Default,,0,0,0,,即使你有一个条件\NSo, even if, let's say, you have a condition,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.52,0:19:58.37,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你从不同的噪声开始 比如另一次生成时从一个不同的噪声开始\Nif you start from noise that is different, let's say, from another generation,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.37,0:20:02.55,Default,,0,0,0,,仅仅因为起始点不同\Nyou will be able to end up with a different end image,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.55,0:20:05.37,Default,,0,0,0,,你就能得到不同的最终图像\Njust because the starting point is different.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.37,0:20:08.89,Default,,0,0,0,,因此 第二个原因是 噪声能引入一些随机性\NSo, the second reason, it introduces some randomness.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.05,0:20:12.52,Default,,0,0,0,,第三个原因是\NAnd then, the third one is,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.52,0:20:19.87,Default,,0,0,0,,我提到过 我们用的噪声分布基本就是高斯分布\Nas I mentioned, noise is basically equal to a Gaussian distribution,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.87,0:20:25.11,Default,,0,0,0,,高斯分布恰好有非常好的数学性质\Nand that distribution just happens to have very nice properties.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.11,0:20:27.36,Default,,0,0,0,,它能极大地简化数学推导\NSo, it simplifies a lot of the math.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.36,0:20:31.99,Default,,0,0,0,,我们会在扩散中看到这一点\NAnd we will see a little bit how that is the case in the diffusion case.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.21,0:20:34.77,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NCool.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.77,0:20:39.29,Default,,0,0,0,,直觉上 噪声是一个好的起始点 大家能理解吗？\NSo, intuitively, does that make sense, that noise is a good starting point?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.29,0:20:42.49,Default,,0,0,0,,都能理解吧？很好\NYeah? OK, cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.49,0:20:45.40,Default,,0,0,0,,我们再来做个很直观的类比\NAnd just to complete that intuition,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.40,0:20:52.57,Default,,0,0,0,,在3D世界中 雕塑家是如何雕刻他们的作品的呢\Nin the 3D world, how sculptors go about sculpting their sculptures,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.57,0:20:57.07,Default,,0,0,0,,他们从一块石头开始\Nthey start with some rock.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.07,0:21:02.39,Default,,0,0,0,,你可以把这块石头想象成一个形状有些粗糙的东西\NAnd you can think of this rock as having shapes that are a little bit noisy.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.39,0:21:06.99,Default,,0,0,0,,这不是你定义的一块石头 这就是一个随机拿到的石头\NIt's not something that you are defining. It's something that is just there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.99,0:21:10.81,Default,,0,0,0,,不同石头的形状也互不相同\NAnd that will be different from a rock to another.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.81,0:21:13.56,Default,,0,0,0,,我喜欢的一个类比是\NSo, one analogy that I like to think of is
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.56,0:21:16.95,Default,,0,0,0,,图像生成过程有点像\Nthis image generation process is a little bit like
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.95,0:21:21.96,Default,,0,0,0,,你是一个雕塑家 你想用石头雕刻出一个物品\Nif you were a sculptor, and you wanted to sculpt from rock.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.96,0:21:25.41,Default,,0,0,0,,我这里把Michelangelo的这句名言留给你们\NSo, yeah, I will leave you with that quote from Michelangelo
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.41,0:21:28.84,Default,,0,0,0,,我觉得这句名言很好地反映了这个思想\Nthat I think also reflects that pretty well.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.47,0:21:31.41,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NCool.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.21,0:21:33.31,Default,,0,0,0,,请问？\NYeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.44,0:22:05.59,Default,,0,0,0,,你说的均匀指的是从相同的状态开始吗？比如从白色画布开始？\NSo, when you say uniform, you mean the same thing? Like, let's say blank?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.59,0:22:09.16,Default,,0,0,0,,好的 他的问题是 为什么我们要从噪声开始\NYeah, so, the question is, why do you want to start from noise,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.16,0:22:14.45,Default,,0,0,0,,而不是从某个预定义的东西开始 比如从白色画布开始？\Nbut not from something that is predefined, let's say, a white canvas, let's say.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.93,0:22:15.84,Default,,0,0,0,,这是个很好的问题\NSo, yeah, great question.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.84,0:22:20.95,Default,,0,0,0,,你会看到 最终使得...\NSo, you will see that what makes the end...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.95,0:22:23.48,Default,,0,0,0,,生成过程本身\NSo, the generation process
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.48,0:22:28.13,Default,,0,0,0,,有时候会引入一些随机性\Nsometimes involves some randomness in the generation process,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.13,0:22:30.16,Default,,0,0,0,,有时候不会引入随机性\Nsometimes it does not.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.16,0:22:34.19,Default,,0,0,0,,此时 随机性只能来自于起始点\NThe randomness is something that occurs at the starting points.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.19,0:22:40.41,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你总是从同一个起始点开始\NSo, if you were to always start your process from the same starting point,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.41,0:22:46.99,Default,,0,0,0,,而其他一切过程都不引入任何随机性\Ngiven that everything else does not introduce some amount of randomness,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.99,0:22:51.72,Default,,0,0,0,,你将永远得到同一个终点\Nyou will always end up at the same endpoint.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.11,0:22:55.96,Default,,0,0,0,,所以某种意义上说 你想要的是\NSo, in a sense, what you want is
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.96,0:22:59.47,Default,,0,0,0,,在某个地方引入一些变化\Nto have some variation introduced somewhere
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.47,0:23:01.87,Default,,0,0,0,,以免总是到达同一个地方\Nin order to not always end up at the same place.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.87,0:23:06.88,Default,,0,0,0,,让我来举个例子 这个“正在阅读一本书的泰迪熊”\NSo, I'll give you an example, This “teddy bear reading a book”.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.88,0:23:14.27,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你用一个生成过程完全没有随机性的范式来生成这样图像\NIf you use a generation paradigm that does not have any stochasticity in its process,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.27,0:23:17.92,Default,,0,0,0,,那么 如果你总是从同一个点开始\Nthen, if you always start from the same point,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.92,0:23:20.85,Default,,0,0,0,,你就总是到达同一个终点\Nthen, you will always end up at the same endpoint,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.85,0:23:24.60,Default,,0,0,0,,这可能不是你想要的效果 你可能更希望获得多样的生成结果\Nand that's probably not something that you want, just for diversity purposes.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.60,0:23:26.03,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是这里的直觉\NSo, that's the intuition.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.28,0:23:28.63,Default,,0,0,0,,好的 很好的问题\NYeah, great question.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.35,0:23:32.23,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NCool.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.16,0:23:41.44,Default,,0,0,0,,我们将在这节课重点关注一篇里程碑式的论文\NOK, so, what we'll focus on for this lecture is a landmark paper
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.44,0:23:46.35,Default,,0,0,0,,这篇论文叫DDPM 我会深入讲解这篇论文的内容\Nthat I will talk a lot in depth, that's called DDPM.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.47,0:23:49.37,Default,,0,0,0,,这是第一篇\NThat was the first
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.37,0:23:56.80,Default,,0,0,0,,把扩散范式成功应用于图像生成的论文\Nthat applying this diffusion paradigm for images in a successful way.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:56.80,0:24:03.99,Default,,0,0,0,,我们将讲解具体是什么原因使得这种方法变得如此有效\NSo, what we're going to do is to go through what makes this approach work so well,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.99,0:24:09.91,Default,,0,0,0,,以及通向最终损失函数的底层机制\Nand the underlying mechanisms that lead to the loss function that we have.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.91,0:24:12.29,Default,,0,0,0,,具体来说\NSo, in particular,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:12.29,0:24:19.68,Default,,0,0,0,,我们的想法是 我们想要生成新的图像\Nthe idea that we have here is what we want is to generate new images.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:19.68,0:24:24.24,Default,,0,0,0,,我们拥有的是一组训练图像\NSo, what we do have is a set of training images.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:26.00,0:24:31.40,Default,,0,0,0,,我们的目标是 如果从噪声开始\NAnd our goal is if we were to start from noise,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:31.40,0:24:35.24,Default,,0,0,0,,我们怎么能够还原出这些图像？\Nhow would we be able to recover those images?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:35.24,0:24:37.65,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是我们想要学习的生成过程\NThat's what we want to learn,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.65,0:24:42.53,Default,,0,0,0,,因为正如我前面提到的 在生成过程中\Nbecause as I mentioned, during our generation process,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:42.53,0:24:47.80,Default,,0,0,0,,我们的策略是 从噪声开始 最终得到清晰图像\Nour strategy is to start from noise and end up with a clean image.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.80,0:24:49.51,Default,,0,0,0,,所以在这里 我们想做的是\NSo here, what we want to do is
Dialogue: 0,0:24:49.51,0:24:56.88,Default,,0,0,0,,用这些训练图像来学习去噪过程\Nto use those training set images to learn that denoising process.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:58.09,0:25:04.23,Default,,0,0,0,,这里涉及两个拥有特定名称的过程\NSo, in that regard, we have two processes that have a very particular name.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:04.23,0:25:07.04,Default,,0,0,0,,第一个过程叫做前向过程\NSo, the first one is called the forward process
Dialogue: 0,0:25:08.32,0:25:15.44,Default,,0,0,0,,就是取训练集中的一张图像\Nthat amounts to taking an image from your training set,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:15.44,0:25:22.23,Default,,0,0,0,,然后对这张图像进行破坏 添加噪声\Nand you are actually corrupting that image. You're adding some noise.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:22.23,0:25:27.80,Default,,0,0,0,,在这里 你定义了某个流程\NSo here, you have some process that you define
Dialogue: 0,0:25:27.80,0:25:33.63,Default,,0,0,0,,这个流程从某个图像x_\{t-1\}开始\Nthat goes from some image x_\{t-1\},
Dialogue: 0,0:25:33.63,0:25:38.91,Default,,0,0,0,,通过添加一些噪声来生成图像x_t\Nand then produces an image x_t by adding some noise.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:40.60,0:25:43.80,Default,,0,0,0,,强调一下 这是你定义的一个流程\NSo again, this is a process that you define.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:43.80,0:25:47.37,Default,,0,0,0,,你知道前向过程中的这个q是什么\NSo, you know what q is in the forward process.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:48.33,0:25:51.53,Default,,0,0,0,,你想做的是\NAnd what you want to do is
Dialogue: 0,0:25:51.53,0:25:57.91,Default,,0,0,0,,从那个非常容易采样的噪声分布开始\Nto start from that noise distribution that is so easy to sample,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.91,0:26:01.65,Default,,0,0,0,,经过反向过程\Nand then, go through the reverse process
Dialogue: 0,0:26:01.65,0:26:09.87,Default,,0,0,0,,对样本去噪 最终回到清晰图像\Nto actually denoise that sample back to the clean space.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:11.59,0:26:16.28,Default,,0,0,0,,你想学习的是一个模型\NAnd so, what you want to learn is a model,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:16.28,0:26:20.60,Default,,0,0,0,,我们用参数θ来表示这个模型的参数\Nthat is something we will characterize with the parameters θ.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:20.60,0:26:30.43,Default,,0,0,0,,你想学习的是如何从带噪图像变成不那么带噪的图像\NWhat you want to learn is how you would go from a noisy image to a less noisy one.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:33.75,0:26:37.84,Default,,0,0,0,,你可能会想\NSo, you may wonder, OK,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:37.84,0:26:42.36,Default,,0,0,0,,你提到了x_t 但我们不知道x_t是什么\Nso, you're talking about x_t, but we don't know what is x_t.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.36,0:26:44.72,Default,,0,0,0,,其实x_t就是一张带噪图像\NIt's just a noisy image.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:44.72,0:26:48.37,Default,,0,0,0,,那你一开始怎么表示图像呢？\NHow do you go about just representing images in the first place?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.04,0:26:56.25,Default,,0,0,0,,我们这里给出一种表示图像的方式\NSo here, we will just see one way of representing images.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:56.25,0:26:59.67,Default,,0,0,0,,这不是人们表示图像的常见方式\NThat is not the way people usually go about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:59.67,0:27:03.03,Default,,0,0,0,,我们将在第4节课更深入地讨论图像表示方式\NThat's something that we'll go more in depth in Lecture 4.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.03,0:27:09.05,Default,,0,0,0,,但我想告诉你在这个框架下要怎么表示图像\NBut I just want to tell you how you would try to represent images in this framework.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:09.05,0:27:15.35,Default,,0,0,0,,正如你所知道的那样 一张图像由像素组成\NSo, as you know, an image is composed of pixels.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:15.35,0:27:19.04,Default,,0,0,0,,有一个高度和一个宽度\NSo, you have a height, and you have a width.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:20.65,0:27:28.15,Default,,0,0,0,,每个像素由3个值组成：红、绿、蓝\NSo, each pixel is actually composed of 3 values, red, green, and blue.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.15,0:27:31.83,Default,,0,0,0,,如此一来 图像就能够覆盖各种颜色\NAnd this allows you to cover a number of colors.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:33.44,0:27:38.93,Default,,0,0,0,,基于此 你可以把图像表示成\NSo, based on that, you can represent your image
Dialogue: 0,0:27:38.93,0:27:43.83,Default,,0,0,0,,由组成图像的所有像素所定义的一个函数\Nas a function of all the pixels that are composing that image,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:43.83,0:27:50.76,Default,,0,0,0,,每个像素对每种颜色都有一个值\Nwhere each of these pixels contains some value for each of these colors.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.76,0:27:54.55,Default,,0,0,0,,可以把每个像素看作有3个值\NSo, you can think of each pixel as having 3 values,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:54.55,0:27:57.55,Default,,0,0,0,,一个表示红色的值\None that represents the amount of red,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:57.55,0:27:59.35,Default,,0,0,0,,一个表示绿色的值\Nthe other one that represents the amount of green,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.35,0:28:01.47,Default,,0,0,0,,还有一个表示蓝色的值\Nand the other one that represents the amount of blue.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:04.29,0:28:11.44,Default,,0,0,0,,基于此 你就能以向量的方式来表示图像了\NSo, based on that, it is fair to say that you can represent images in a vectorial fashion.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:11.44,0:28:17.95,Default,,0,0,0,,这个示例中图像的维度将等于\NSo here, the dimensionality of the image in this example would be equal to
Dialogue: 0,0:28:17.95,0:28:19.41,Default,,0,0,0,,像素的数量\Nthe number of pixels
Dialogue: 0,0:28:19.41,0:28:24.35,Default,,0,0,0,,乘以每个像素需要表示的维度数量 即乘以3\Ntimes the number of dimensions you need to represent in a pixel, which is 3.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.35,0:28:30.31,Default,,0,0,0,,这个向量有n个维度 n等于像素数乘以3\NSo here, you would have n dimensions, where n is equal to number of pixels times 3.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:31.55,0:28:34.56,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是表示图像的一种方式\NSo, this would be one way to represent your images.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:35.53,0:28:39.63,Default,,0,0,0,,当然 这不是最聪明的图像表示方式\NOf course, this is not the most clever way of representing images,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:39.63,0:28:42.08,Default,,0,0,0,,我们会在第4节课进一步了解图像表示方式\Nand we will see that more in Lecture 4.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:42.08,0:28:44.88,Default,,0,0,0,,但我希望你们记住的是\NBut what I want you to remember is
Dialogue: 0,0:28:44.88,0:28:51.01,Default,,0,0,0,,当我们讨论图像 当我们说到x_0、x_t等等的时候\Nwhen we talk about images here, when we say x_0, x_t and so on,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:51.01,0:28:55.00,Default,,0,0,0,,我们说的实际上是向量\Nwhat we're talking about is actually vectors.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.00,0:28:58.51,Default,,0,0,0,,这些向量是用来表示图像的\NAnd these vectors are the ones that are representing these images.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:01.20,0:29:02.37,Default,,0,0,0,,大家能理解吗？\NMake sense?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.48,0:29:05.08,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NCool.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:05.45,0:29:06.95,Default,,0,0,0,,说到向量\NSo, speaking of vectors.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:06.95,0:29:11.15,Default,,0,0,0,,我说过 概率论是这门课的先修课程\NSo, I told you there is a prerequisite on probability theory.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:11.15,0:29:13.80,Default,,0,0,0,,我这里会介绍一些概率论的基础概念\NSo, I'm just going to cover the basics here.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:14.52,0:29:18.57,Default,,0,0,0,,你可能知道一个常见的分布\NSo, you may know the common distribution,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:18.57,0:29:21.31,Default,,0,0,0,,这个分布叫高斯分布 也叫正态分布\Nthat's called the Gaussian distribution, normal distribution,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:21.31,0:29:23.72,Default,,0,0,0,,高斯分布的随机变量\Nwhere you have some random variable
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.72,0:29:29.72,Default,,0,0,0,,是依均值为μ 方差为σ^2的高斯分布采样得到的\Nthat is drawn from a distribution of mean μ and then variance σ^2.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:30.72,0:29:35.04,Default,,0,0,0,,我们同样可以定义向量的高斯分布\NWell, you can have the same thing for vectors.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:36.48,0:29:40.20,Default,,0,0,0,,所有论文都假设你已经知道这些基础知识了\NSo, I know all these papers they assume you know that.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:40.20,0:29:41.95,Default,,0,0,0,,但在读论文时 你可能对有些基础知识还不太清楚\NWhen you read, it's not super clear.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.95,0:29:43.80,Default,,0,0,0,,我这里就是想强调一下涉及的基础知识\NSo, I just want to emphasize.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:43.80,0:29:48.59,Default,,0,0,0,,随机变量也可以是向量\NYou can also have random variables that are vectors.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:48.59,0:29:51.81,Default,,0,0,0,,在这种情况下 你会有一个向量\NAnd in this case, you will have a vector
Dialogue: 0,0:29:51.81,0:29:57.68,Default,,0,0,0,,这个向量是依某个均值的分布采样得到的 而均值本身也是一个向量\Nthat is drawn from a distribution of some mean, and the mean is a vector,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:57.68,0:30:04.24,Default,,0,0,0,,分布中还有一个方差 我们用协方差矩阵来表示方差\Nand then, some variance, which is actually represented by a covariance matrix.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:06.43,0:30:10.07,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你不了解协方差矩阵 那也不用担心\NSo, don't worry if you don't know about the covariance matrix,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:10.07,0:30:12.44,Default,,0,0,0,,因为大多数时候\Nbecause most of the time,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:12.44,0:30:21.29,Default,,0,0,0,,我们会把协方差矩阵简化为方差乘以单位矩阵\Nwe actually simplify the covariance matrix to be a variance times the identity.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:21.29,0:30:24.21,Default,,0,0,0,,我们把满足这种形式的高斯分布称为...\NAnd we call this formulation actually...
Dialogue: 0,0:30:24.21,0:30:27.60,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是各向同性高斯分布\NSo, these are like isotropic Gaussians,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:27.60,0:30:29.71,Default,,0,0,0,,因为这意味着\Nbecause what that means is that
Dialogue: 0,0:30:29.71,0:30:33.87,Default,,0,0,0,,数据在所有方向上的变化是相同的\Nthe variation of the data across all directions is the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:35.05,0:30:38.15,Default,,0,0,0,,所以大多数时候 为了简化数学描述\NSo, most of the time, to just simplify the math,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:38.15,0:30:43.99,Default,,0,0,0,,我们会假设协方差等于σ^2·I\Nwhat we will assume is that the covariance is actually equal to σ^2·I,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:43.99,0:30:48.23,Default,,0,0,0,,就是你在这里看到的对角矩阵\Nwhich is the diagonal matrix, which you see here,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:48.23,0:30:51.33,Default,,0,0,0,,而不是那个超级复杂的协方差矩阵\Nand not the super complicated covariance matrix.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:52.99,0:30:56.77,Default,,0,0,0,,顺便问一下 大家还记得协方差是什么吗？\NSo, by the way, do you remember what covariance is roughly?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:56.77,0:30:58.64,Default,,0,0,0,,让我快速回顾一下这个基础知识\NSo, maybe I can just recap.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:58.64,0:31:00.39,Default,,0,0,0,,什么是协方差？\NSo, what is covariance?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:00.39,0:31:03.24,Default,,0,0,0,,协方差是\NSo, covariance is
Dialogue: 0,0:31:03.24,0:31:10.31,Default,,0,0,0,,用来衡量两个随机变量如何线性共变的一个量\Na quantity that quantifies how two random variables vary in a linear way.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:11.31,0:31:16.05,Default,,0,0,0,,当然 协方差有相应的数学表达式 但这是协方差大概的直觉思想\NOf course, there is some mathematical expression, but this is like the general intuition.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:18.28,0:31:21.71,Default,,0,0,0,,说到直觉\NSo, speaking of intuition,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:21.71,0:31:29.00,Default,,0,0,0,,当我们说一个分布是各向同性的 意思就是协方差等于σ^2·I\Nwhen we say that a distribution is isotropic, this is what we mean.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:29.00,0:31:34.55,Default,,0,0,0,,意思是方差在所有方向上都相同\NWe mean that the variance is the same across all directions.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:34.55,0:31:41.07,Default,,0,0,0,,你可以想象分布像是一个圆 颜色代表概率密度\NSo, you can think of it as some circle where the color represents the density.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:43.31,0:31:44.45,Default,,0,0,0,,没问题吧？\NYeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:45.80,0:31:46.93,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NOK, cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:47.32,0:31:49.95,Default,,0,0,0,,高斯分布很好的一点是\NAnd of course, what's great about Gaussians is
Dialogue: 0,0:31:49.95,0:31:53.61,Default,,0,0,0,,它有一个非常简洁的解析表达式\Nyou also have an analytical expression that's quite simple
Dialogue: 0,0:31:53.61,0:31:56.32,Default,,0,0,0,,高斯分布的概率密度函数非常简洁\Nabout the probability density function.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.32,0:32:02.55,Default,,0,0,0,,我把高斯分布的概率密度函数放在幻灯片上 此函数计算起来很方便 很不错\NSo, I'm just putting this here, and it's easy to compute. That's great.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:04.04,0:32:07.52,Default,,0,0,0,,回到我们所说的噪声\NSo, going back to what we call noise.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:07.52,0:32:13.72,Default,,0,0,0,,我们已经看到 图像可以用向量来表示\NSo here, we saw that images can be represented by vectors.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:13.72,0:32:17.76,Default,,0,0,0,,当我们说采样噪声时\NSo, when we say we sample from noise,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:17.76,0:32:24.01,Default,,0,0,0,,我们的意思是依标准正态分布采样\Nwe will say here that we actually sample from a standard normal distribution.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:25.88,0:32:28.09,Default,,0,0,0,,我们通常把采样得到的噪声记作ε\NSo, we usually note that ε.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:28.09,0:32:32.80,Default,,0,0,0,,这里的ε是依均值为0的正态分布采样得到的\NSo, ε will be drawn from a normal distribution of mean 0.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.80,0:32:37.31,Default,,0,0,0,,这里的0实际上是0向量\NSo, 0 is actually the vector, the 0 vector.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:37.31,0:32:42.56,Default,,0,0,0,,采样所用的协方差就是单位矩阵\NAnd then, the covariance will actually be the identity matrix.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:44.84,0:32:45.64,Default,,0,0,0,,请问？\NYeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:46.69,0:32:47.65,Default,,0,0,0,,好的\NYeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:58.12,0:33:00.44,Default,,0,0,0,,这是一个好问题 这是一个很好的问题\NIt's a great question. It's a great question.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.44,0:33:03.91,Default,,0,0,0,,他的问题是 这里的表示是连续的还是离散的？\NSo, the question is, is the representation continuous or discrete?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:03.91,0:33:09.73,Default,,0,0,0,,我们之前说的像素值是离散的 0、1、2 一直到255\NSo, we talked about pixel values that were discrete, 0, 1, 2 until 255.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.73,0:33:15.52,Default,,0,0,0,,但在实践中 像素值会被缩放到-1和1之间\NBut in practice, these are actually scaled between, let's say, -1 and 1,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:15.52,0:33:18.23,Default,,0,0,0,,或者说更接近是浮点数\Nor some value that's more of a float.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:18.23,0:33:21.16,Default,,0,0,0,,所以 你可以假定像素值实际上是连续的\NSo, you can assume that these are actually continuous.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.83,0:33:27.31,Default,,0,0,0,,是的 不过你可以假定像素值实际上是连续的\NRight, but you can assume it's actually continuous, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.07,0:33:28.91,Default,,0,0,0,,是的\NYeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:32.28,0:33:33.79,Default,,0,0,0,,是的 是的\NRight, right.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.44,0:33:37.55,Default,,0,0,0,,我们总会引入一些假设\NSo, there's always some assumption.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:37.55,0:33:45.20,Default,,0,0,0,,在这里 当我们说像素之间没有相关性时...\NAnd so, here, at least, when you say there is no correlation between pixels...
Dialogue: 0,0:33:45.20,0:33:49.00,Default,,0,0,0,,我们这里说的实际上是噪声之间没有相关性\NSo here, we actually mean the noise.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:49.00,0:33:51.60,Default,,0,0,0,,我们确实是随机采样的噪声\NSo, noise, we actually just sample at random.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:51.60,0:33:54.71,Default,,0,0,0,,是的 是的 对于真实图像来说 各个像素之间会有相关性\NSo, yeah, yeah. It's not true for actual images, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:54.71,0:33:55.64,Default,,0,0,0,,不 确实不是\NNo, it's not true.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:55.64,0:33:57.84,Default,,0,0,0,,好的 很好的问题\NYeah, yeah. Great questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:59.81,0:34:00.61,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NOK, cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:00.61,0:34:03.56,Default,,0,0,0,,我看了一下时间 我知道还有很多内容要讲\NI'm just looking at the time, and I know we have a lot of content.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:03.56,0:34:05.77,Default,,0,0,0,,所以我会稍微加快一点\NSo, I'll just go a little bit faster.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:05.77,0:34:09.41,Default,,0,0,0,,我想确认一下 目前的速度还好吗？\NJust want to know if the pace so far is good?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:09.41,0:34:11.59,Default,,0,0,0,,我不想让大家觉得跟不上课程内容\NYeah, OK, I don't want to lose you,
Dialogue: 0,0:34:11.59,0:34:12.24,Default,,0,0,0,,因为我认为\Nbecause I think
Dialogue: 0,0:34:12.24,0:34:19.96,Default,,0,0,0,,虽然这是第1节课 但这节课涉及的数学内容可能是整个课程里最难的\Nthis is the first lecture that is maybe the most difficult in terms of flat math.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:19.96,0:34:22.77,Default,,0,0,0,,最难的一节课正好排在开头 确实有点不巧\NSo, it's just kind of sad that this is the first lecture.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.37,0:34:26.07,Default,,0,0,0,,但没关系 我们继续\NBut yeah, let's continue.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:26.07,0:34:32.55,Default,,0,0,0,,正如我提到的 我们想做的是取清晰图像然后加噪\NSo, as I mentioned, what we want to do is to take clean images and to corrupt them.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:32.55,0:34:37.83,Default,,0,0,0,,我们要做的是 取一张可能已经加过噪的图像\NSo, what we do is we take some image that maybe we have noised,
Dialogue: 0,0:34:37.83,0:34:39.53,Default,,0,0,0,,然后再加一些噪声\Nand we add some noise.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:40.55,0:34:45.73,Default,,0,0,0,,实际上 我们给图像加的噪声是带权重的\NAnd we actually add these quantities in a weighted fashion.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:47.08,0:34:53.28,Default,,0,0,0,,这些权重是由我们自己定义的\NAnd these weights are actually defined by us.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:54.80,0:34:59.56,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你还记得 我们这里提到的q\NSo, if you remember, when we talked about q,
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.56,0:35:02.84,Default,,0,0,0,,就是我们为前向过程定义的那个q\Nthe process that we defined for the forward process,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:02.84,0:35:04.79,Default,,0,0,0,,这个q实际上是我们自己定义的\Nis actually something that we define.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:06.35,0:35:09.33,Default,,0,0,0,,我们就是这样对图像加噪的\NSo, this is how we noise images.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:09.33,0:35:10.51,Default,,0,0,0,,我们取一张图像\NSo, we take an image.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:10.51,0:35:13.72,Default,,0,0,0,,依正态分布采样一些噪声\NWe take some noise from a distribution, from the normal distribution.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:13.72,0:35:19.60,Default,,0,0,0,,接下来 我们对两者做加权平均 权重稍后会讲到\NAnd then, we do a weighted average with some weights that we will see.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:19.60,0:35:20.93,Default,,0,0,0,,说到权重\NAnd speaking of those,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:20.93,0:35:27.32,Default,,0,0,0,,你会听到一个在所有论文中反复出现的术语 噪声调度\Nyou will hear of a recurring term across all papers, noise schedule.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:27.32,0:35:30.47,Default,,0,0,0,,噪声调度指的就是\NSo, the noise schedule is actually referring to
Dialogue: 0,0:35:30.47,0:35:37.04,Default,,0,0,0,,你在噪声值上乘以的那些系数\Nthe coefficients here that you use to multiply these values.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:37.04,0:35:39.32,Default,,0,0,0,,之所以叫调度 是因为在某些时间点\NSo, it's a schedule because at some point,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:39.32,0:35:42.76,Default,,0,0,0,,你加的噪声可能比其他时间点少\Nyou may add maybe less noise than some other points.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:44.97,0:35:46.08,Default,,0,0,0,,没问题吧？\NYeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:47.39,0:35:48.12,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NOK. Great.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:48.12,0:35:51.76,Default,,0,0,0,,让我们更深入一点数学\NSo, let's go a little bit more into the math.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:53.12,0:35:57.80,Default,,0,0,0,,我们从x_0开始\NSo, we start from x_0.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:58.77,0:36:04.15,Default,,0,0,0,,我们的加噪方法是\NAnd then, the way we go about adding noise is
Dialogue: 0,0:36:04.15,0:36:09.51,Default,,0,0,0,,我们有已经定义好的前向过程q\Nwe have our forward process that we've defined q,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:11.09,0:36:16.67,Default,,0,0,0,,过程q实际上是依正态分布采样\Nwhich is actually something we will draw from a normal distribution.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:18.07,0:36:21.35,Default,,0,0,0,,我们可以把噪声量表示为...\NSo, we can express the quantity...
Dialogue: 0,0:36:21.35,0:36:27.27,Default,,0,0,0,,即q(x_t|x_\{t-1\}) 也就是从噪声较少的图像到噪声较多的图像\NSo, q(x_t|x_\{t-1\}), so, the noisier image compared to the less noisy image as
Dialogue: 0,0:36:27.27,0:36:34.53,Default,,0,0,0,,是一个以噪声较少的图像为中心定义的正态分布乘以某个系数\Na normal distribution centered on that less noisy image with some coefficient,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:34.53,0:36:36.85,Default,,0,0,0,,再加上一些噪声\Nwhere you add some noise,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:36.85,0:36:41.87,Default,,0,0,0,,噪声由协方差矩阵β_t·I来表示\Nwhich is something that is represented by the covariance matrix β_t·I.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:45.25,0:36:46.71,Default,,0,0,0,,没问题吧？\NYeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:46.71,0:36:47.71,Default,,0,0,0,,这意味着...\NSo, what that means is...
Dialogue: 0,0:36:47.71,0:36:50.64,Default,,0,0,0,,我可以把加噪过程重写为...\NI'm just going to rewrite this in a very...
Dialogue: 0,0:36:50.64,0:36:52.80,Default,,0,0,0,,加噪过程就是这样的\NSo, it's just what that means.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:52.80,0:37:14.44,Default,,0,0,0,,即x_t=√(1-β_t)x_\{t-1\}+√(β_t)ε 其中ε~N(0,I), right?\NSo, it's x_t=√(1-β_t)x_\{t-1\}+√(β_t)ε, ε~N(0,I).
Dialogue: 0,0:37:14.44,0:37:20.07,Default,,0,0,0,,这个看似复杂的数学公式其实就是\NSo, this seemingly math formula is just nothing else than just
Dialogue: 0,0:37:20.07,0:37:24.85,Default,,0,0,0,,你取噪声较少的图像 乘以某个系数\Nyou taking your less noisy image, weighting that by some coefficient,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:24.85,0:37:28.00,Default,,0,0,0,,然后加上一些噪声 乘以某个系数\Nand then, adding some noise with some coefficient.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:29.87,0:37:33.05,Default,,0,0,0,,现在你可能会问 为什么用这些特定的系数？\NNow you may wonder why are you using these coefficients?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:33.05,0:37:36.09,Default,,0,0,0,,在后面的课程中 我们会讲为什么这么做\NSo, we will see later in the class why we do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:36.09,0:37:37.25,Default,,0,0,0,,但你可以看到\NBut you can see that
Dialogue: 0,0:37:37.25,0:37:43.45,Default,,0,0,0,,整个表达式的方差从这一步到下一步是保持不变的\Nthe variance of this whole thing is preserved from one step to another.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:43.45,0:37:51.35,Default,,0,0,0,,这种加噪方式被称为方差保持（VP）\NSo, you will see that this way of noising images is called Variance-Preserving, VP.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:52.51,0:37:54.13,Default,,0,0,0,,我们之后会更详细地展开讨论\NWe'll see that more later on.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:57.08,0:37:58.17,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NOK, cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:59.97,0:38:02.61,Default,,0,0,0,,说到噪声调度\NSo, speaking of the noise schedule.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:02.61,0:38:08.16,Default,,0,0,0,,这些β_t通常不是均匀的 而是变化的\NSo, these β_t are not typically uniform, they're varying.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:08.16,0:38:15.32,Default,,0,0,0,,DDPM论文把β_t定义为逐渐递增\NAnd the way they are defined in the DDPM paper is they're gradually increased,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:15.32,0:38:18.77,Default,,0,0,0,,也就是你从清晰图像开始\Nas in you will start from your clean image,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:18.77,0:38:21.56,Default,,0,0,0,,先加一点点噪声\Nand you will just add a little bit of noise,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:21.56,0:38:24.73,Default,,0,0,0,,然后再多加一点噪声 再多加一点噪声\Nand then, maybe a little bit more, and again and again,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:24.73,0:38:27.85,Default,,0,0,0,,到最后 加的噪声会大得多\Nand then, at the end, you will have much bigger noise.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:27.85,0:38:30.33,Default,,0,0,0,,这么做的原因是\NAnd the reason why people do that is because
Dialogue: 0,0:38:30.33,0:38:33.47,Default,,0,0,0,,当接近清晰图像时\Nwhen you're close to the clean image,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:33.47,0:38:36.80,Default,,0,0,0,,你更关心的是学习到图像的一些细节\Nwhat you care about is to learn those little details,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:37.84,0:38:40.91,Default,,0,0,0,,但当更接近噪声时\Nbut when you're closer to the noise,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:40.91,0:38:44.72,Default,,0,0,0,,你更关心的是学习到图像的大致形状\Nwhat you care more about learning is the general shape of the image.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:46.16,0:38:51.36,Default,,0,0,0,,因此 噪声调度对模型的学习能力会起到非常重要的作用\NSo, this noise schedule is actually quite important in our ability to learn.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:51.36,0:38:53.71,Default,,0,0,0,,这是提高模型学习能力的一种做法\NAnd it's just one way of doing things.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:55.63,0:38:57.03,Default,,0,0,0,,没问题吧？\NYeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:57.03,0:38:59.99,Default,,0,0,0,,正如你所见 β_t属于0和1之间\NAnd as you can tell, it's between 0 and 1,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:59.99,0:39:04.00,Default,,0,0,0,,否则平方根下面会出现负数\Nwell, because, otherwise, you would have a negative value in the square root.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:06.29,0:39:07.51,Default,,0,0,0,,很好 我们继续\NCool. Moving on.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:07.51,0:39:12.33,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你这样定义前向过程\NSo, if you define your process like this,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:14.31,0:39:20.79,Default,,0,0,0,,那么事实证明 你不需要按顺序逐个步骤加噪\Nthen, it turns out you don't need to noise your images in a sequential way
Dialogue: 0,0:39:20.79,0:39:24.80,Default,,0,0,0,,才能得到步骤t的加噪结果\Nin order to get the number t.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:24.80,0:39:29.32,Default,,0,0,0,,你可以直接从清晰图像跳到步骤t\NYou can actually go directly from your clean image to the step number t.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:32.24,0:39:35.04,Default,,0,0,0,,你能看出该怎么做吗？\NDo you see how you would do that?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:36.69,0:39:43.57,Default,,0,0,0,,也许不那么明显 但我前面提到过 高斯分布有很好的性质\NMaybe it's not super obvious, but I told you that Gaussians had very nice properties.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:43.57,0:39:49.52,Default,,0,0,0,,这里 ε是依高斯分布采样的噪声\NSo here, ε, the noise is drawn from a Gaussian distribution.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:49.52,0:39:51.43,Default,,0,0,0,,如果我们重写这个公式...\NSo, if you were to rewrite...
Dialogue: 0,0:39:51.43,0:40:00.83,Default,,0,0,0,,首先 我定义α_t 它等于1-β_t\NSo, first of all, I will just define α_t, which is just equal to 1-β_t.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:00.83,0:40:04.13,Default,,0,0,0,,这只是在进行重参数化\NIt is just a reparameterization.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:04.13,0:40:08.03,Default,,0,0,0,,这里就变成了1-α_t\NSo here, it will be 1-α_t.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:08.03,0:40:17.95,Default,,0,0,0,,这里 我们可以用相同的公式来替换x_\{t-1\}\NSo here, what we're saying is, x_\{t-1\}, we can also use the same formula,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:17.95,0:40:33.67,Default,,0,0,0,,也就是等于√(α_\{t-1\})x_\{t-2\}+√(1-α_\{t-1\})ε_\{t-1\}\Nwhich will be equal to √(α_\{t-1\})x_\{t-2\}+√(1-α_\{t-1\})ε_\{t-1\}.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:33.67,0:40:36.37,Default,,0,0,0,,这些噪声是独立的\NSo, these noises are independent.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:38.32,0:40:51.45,Default,,0,0,0,,如果要把x_t表示为x_\{t-2\}和ε的函数 你会怎么做？\NSo, if you were to express x_t as a function of x_\{t-2\} and ε's, what would you do?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:52.95,0:40:57.61,Default,,0,0,0,,我这里我要把x_t展开\NSo here, I'm just going to expand x_t.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:57.61,0:41:00.40,Default,,0,0,0,,我们在这里加个中括号\NSo here, I'm just in parentheses.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:01.89,0:41:06.83,Default,,0,0,0,,因此 x_t等于√(α_t)...\NSo, it's equal to √(α_t)...
Dialogue: 0,0:41:07.97,0:41:12.85,Default,,0,0,0,,我直接用√(α_t)乘以中括号里的项\NSo, I'm directly going to multiply this quantity by the one that we have here.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:13.96,0:41:48.83,Default,,0,0,0,,因此 x_t等于√(α_t·α_\{t-1\})x_\{t-2\}+√(α_t(1-α_\{t-1\}))ε_\{t-1\}+...\NSo, it's √(α_t·α_\{t-1\})x_\{t-2\}+√(α_t(1-α_\{t-1\}))ε_\{t-1\}+...
Dialogue: 0,0:41:48.83,0:41:51.45,Default,,0,0,0,,顺便说一下 我这里做的就是很基本的数学运算\NSo, by the way, I'm just doing some math, very basic math.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:53.53,0:42:01.01,Default,,0,0,0,,+√(1-α_t)ε_t\N+√(1-α_t)ε_t.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:02.95,0:42:04.24,Default,,0,0,0,,到这里还清楚吗？\NSo far so good?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:05.60,0:42:12.11,Default,,0,0,0,,这是我们的第一项 没问题\NOK, so here, we have our first term. No problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:12.11,0:42:14.76,Default,,0,0,0,,这里我们得到的是\NThen, what we have is
Dialogue: 0,0:42:14.76,0:42:20.24,Default,,0,0,0,,依高斯分布采样的随机变量的加权和\Na weighted sum of random variables drawn from a Gaussian distribution.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:21.53,0:42:27.24,Default,,0,0,0,,我跟你们说过 高斯分布有很好的性质\NSo, I told you that these Gaussian distributions had very nice properties.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:27.24,0:42:31.72,Default,,0,0,0,,事实上 如果你有两个独立的随机变量\NSo, it turns out that if you have two random variables
Dialogue: 0,0:42:31.72,0:42:35.99,Default,,0,0,0,,且这两个随机变量都依高斯分布采样\Nthat are independent and drawn from a Gaussian distribution,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:35.99,0:42:37.75,Default,,0,0,0,,你可以得到的是\Nso, you can really have
Dialogue: 0,0:42:37.75,0:42:44.96,Default,,0,0,0,,这两项等于这两个高斯分布的标准差组合\Nthis as being equal to the standard deviation of this quantity
Dialogue: 0,0:42:44.96,0:42:50.85,Default,,0,0,0,,乘以一个同样依高斯分布采样的随机变量\Ntimes a random variable that is also drawn from a Gaussian distribution.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:52.31,0:42:54.65,Default,,0,0,0,,怎么把方差加起来？\NSo, how do you add this variance?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:54.65,0:42:56.44,Default,,0,0,0,,总方差\NSo, you have the variance of everything
Dialogue: 0,0:42:56.44,0:42:59.52,Default,,0,0,0,,等于第一个的方差加上另一个的方差\Nthat is equal to the variance of 1 plus the variance of other.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:59.52,0:43:03.43,Default,,0,0,0,,从形式上看...\NSo here, in terms of how that looks like...
Dialogue: 0,0:43:04.32,0:43:10.39,Default,,0,0,0,,这里我们得到的方差等于α_t...\NSo here, you will have the variance that will be equal to α_t...
Dialogue: 0,0:43:10.39,0:43:14.01,Default,,0,0,0,,方差等于这一项的平方加上这一项的平方\NSo, it's basically this squared plus this squared.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:14.01,0:43:25.11,Default,,0,0,0,,方差等于α_t(1-α_\{t-1\})+1-α_t 进一步等于...\NSo, it's α_t(1-α_\{t-1\})+1-α_t, which is equal to...
Dialogue: 0,0:43:25.11,0:43:27.76,Default,,0,0,0,,两个α_t可以消去\NSo, these one go away.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:27.76,0:43:34.21,Default,,0,0,0,,你得到的是1-α_tα_\{t-1\}\NAnd then, you have 1-α_tα_\{t-1\}.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:38.80,0:43:42.60,Default,,0,0,0,,这意味着什么？\NSo, what does that mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:42.60,0:43:57.48,Default,,0,0,0,,这意味着x_t=√(α_tα_\{t-1\})...\NThat means that x_t=√(α_tα_\{t-1\})...
Dialogue: 0,0:43:57.48,0:44:01.15,Default,,0,0,0,,我只是把上面的抄了下来\NSo, I'm just copying what is above.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:01.15,0:44:10.28,Default,,0,0,0,,x_t=√(α_tα_\{t-1\})x_\{t-2\} 加上另一项的标准差\Nx_t=√(α_tα_\{t-1\})x_\{t-2\}, plus the standard deviation of this one,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:10.28,0:44:24.69,Default,,0,0,0,,即√(1-α_tα_\{t-1\})ε 其中ε~N(0,I)\Nwhich is √(1-α_tα_\{t-1\})ε, ε~N(0,I).
Dialogue: 0,0:44:30.25,0:44:35.92,Default,,0,0,0,,这个简要的证明过程要证明的是\NAnd this sketch of a proof is just a way for us to prove that
Dialogue: 0,0:44:35.92,0:44:39.57,Default,,0,0,0,,你确实可以一直级联到步骤0\Nyou can actually cascade these things up to 0.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:41.16,0:44:48.16,Default,,0,0,0,,因此 你可以把步骤t的带噪图像\NAnd therefore, you can have an expression of the noisy image at step t
Dialogue: 0,0:44:48.16,0:44:53.04,Default,,0,0,0,,表示为步骤0清晰图像的函数\Nas a function of the clean image at step 0.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:53.04,0:44:57.63,Default,,0,0,0,,这是一个包含参数ᾱ的函数\NAnd this can be expressed as a function of ᾱ,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:57.63,0:45:04.85,Default,,0,0,0,,其中ᾱ等于所有α_i的乘积\Nwhere ᾱ is equal to the product of the α_i's.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:04.85,0:45:09.00,Default,,0,0,0,,这里 α_t、α_\{t-1\}只是级联一个步骤的结果\NSo here, α_t, α_\{t-1\} is just the start, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:09.00,0:45:12.79,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你继续级联 最终得到的就是所有α_t的乘积\NBut if you continue, it's just the product of all the α_t's.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:15.64,0:45:16.85,Default,,0,0,0,,大家能理解吗？\NDoes that make sense?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:17.77,0:45:21.55,Default,,0,0,0,,我刚才在黑板上写的这些\NSo, what I just wrote on the board is
Dialogue: 0,0:45:21.55,0:45:26.69,Default,,0,0,0,,就是为了让你信服我说的是合理的\Njust a way for you to be convinced that what I'm saying is making sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:26.69,0:45:38.00,Default,,0,0,0,,你可以把x_t表示为x_0的函数 只需把β_t替换成ᾱ_t即可\NSo, you can express x_t as a function of x_0 by just using ᾱ_t instead of this β_t.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:39.95,0:45:40.88,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NCool.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:41.33,0:45:43.53,Default,,0,0,0,,推导中用到了一个性质\NSo, yeah, so, the derivation you use the fact that
Dialogue: 0,0:45:43.53,0:45:46.69,Default,,0,0,0,,独立高斯分布随机变量之和的方差\Nthe variance of the sum of independent Gaussians
Dialogue: 0,0:45:46.69,0:45:49.56,Default,,0,0,0,,等于各自随机变量方差之和\Nis just the sum of the respective variances.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:50.29,0:45:56.12,Default,,0,0,0,,顺便说一下 这门课可以做很多推导\NAnd by the way, there's many derivations we can do in this class.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:56.12,0:45:58.48,Default,,0,0,0,,问题是我们没有时间\NThe problem is we do not have time.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:58.48,0:46:02.77,Default,,0,0,0,,这是第一个推导 所以我写在黑板上了\NSo, here is the first one, which is why I wrote on the blackboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:02.77,0:46:05.07,Default,,0,0,0,,但如果我们没有时间\NBut if we do not have time,
Dialogue: 0,0:46:05.07,0:46:10.44,Default,,0,0,0,,则我们会在幻灯片底部放一个小提示\Nwe will always have a little message at the bottom of the slide
Dialogue: 0,0:46:10.44,0:46:12.89,Default,,0,0,0,,小提示里告诉你用了什么技巧\Nthat just tells you what the trick is.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:14.45,0:46:20.13,Default,,0,0,0,,你可以放心假设 如果课上没推导某个东西\NAnd you can safely assume that if we don't derive this thing in class,
Dialogue: 0,0:46:20.13,0:46:22.73,Default,,0,0,0,,考试也不会考\Nit will not be asked during the exams.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:23.88,0:46:25.05,Default,,0,0,0,,没问题吧？\NOK?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:26.01,0:46:27.05,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NCool.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:27.59,0:46:28.69,Default,,0,0,0,,继续往下\NMoving on.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:28.69,0:46:35.99,Default,,0,0,0,,到目前为止我们做的就是定义了前向过程\NSo, now what we have done is just defined our forward process.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:35.99,0:46:40.44,Default,,0,0,0,,我们还推导了一种方便的方式\NAnd we just also derived a convenient way
Dialogue: 0,0:46:40.44,0:46:48.72,Default,,0,0,0,,可以从步骤0直接到步骤t的加噪结果 不需要经过所有中间步骤\Nto noise our image from step 0 to step t without going through all the steps.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:48.72,0:46:54.00,Default,,0,0,0,,现在我们要看的是\NSo, what we will do now is to see
Dialogue: 0,0:46:54.00,0:46:59.39,Default,,0,0,0,,我们该如何确定去噪过程\Nhow we can actually go about determining the process
Dialogue: 0,0:46:59.39,0:47:02.09,Default,,0,0,0,,也就是如何反转前向过程\Nthat denoises that forward process.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:02.96,0:47:13.37,Default,,0,0,0,,也就是说 我们想知道p_θ(x_\{t-1\}|x_t)是什么\NSo, what we want to is how can we go about seeing what p_θ(x_\{t-1\}|x_t) is.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:15.45,0:47:20.20,Default,,0,0,0,,正如我前面提到的 我们想学习的是p_θ\NSo, as I mentioned, what we want to do is to learn p_θ.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:21.69,0:47:26.69,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你有一些机器学习经验\NSo, in case you have some experience in ML,
Dialogue: 0,0:47:26.69,0:47:30.48,Default,,0,0,0,,你会知道人们常用的一个技巧是\Nyou will see that a common trick that people do is
Dialogue: 0,0:47:30.48,0:47:35.88,Default,,0,0,0,,给定训练数据 我们要做的是\Ngiven some training data, what they want to do is
Dialogue: 0,0:47:35.88,0:47:42.08,Default,,0,0,0,,最大化模型看到训练数据的概率\Nto maximize the probability of your model seeing the training data.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:42.08,0:47:48.35,Default,,0,0,0,,我们想得到θ 以最大化模型看到训练数据的概率\NMaximized, they want to maximize such a probability with respect to θ.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:49.56,0:47:53.04,Default,,0,0,0,,我们想找到参数θ\NSo, they want to find the parameters θ
Dialogue: 0,0:47:53.04,0:47:59.51,Default,,0,0,0,,使得模型看到训练数据的概率达到最大\Nthat maximize the probability of your model of seeing your training data.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:01.95,0:48:06.93,Default,,0,0,0,,在这里 训练数据就是我们的训练图像 即清晰图像\NSo, in this case, training data is just our training images. So, it's clean images.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:06.93,0:48:13.39,Default,,0,0,0,,我们的模型包含p_θ\NAnd then, our model here is something that has p_θ in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:13.39,0:48:19.97,Default,,0,0,0,,p_θ就是某张图像出现的概率 我们之后会讲如何施加条件\NSo, it's the probability of an image happening that we will see how we can condition.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:19.97,0:48:24.25,Default,,0,0,0,,我们要做的是找到能实现这一目标的参数θ\NAnd what we want to do is to find the parameters θ that do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:25.68,0:48:30.71,Default,,0,0,0,,你会发现 每当谈论概率\NSo, you will see that whenever you talk about probabilities,
Dialogue: 0,0:48:30.71,0:48:36.40,Default,,0,0,0,,你总是或大部分时候都在谈论对数概率\Nyou will always or most of the time talk about log probabilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:36.40,0:48:41.85,Default,,0,0,0,,一是因为对数函数有很好的性质\NOne because the logarithm function has pretty nice properties.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:41.85,0:48:47.03,Default,,0,0,0,,二是因为使用对数函数会使计算变得更稳定\NAnd then, the second reason is that it's just computationally more stable,
Dialogue: 0,0:48:47.03,0:48:50.08,Default,,0,0,0,,因为概率值在0和1之间\Nbecause probabilities are between 0 and 1.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:50.08,0:48:54.85,Default,,0,0,0,,如果p的值非常非常小 计算可能会变得不稳定\NSo, if you have very, very small values of p, then it can be a little bit unstable.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:56.76,0:48:59.97,Default,,0,0,0,,在我们确定去噪过程之前\NSo, before we determine that,
Dialogue: 0,0:48:59.97,0:49:07.39,Default,,0,0,0,,我想快速复习一下概率中的一个概念\NI just wanted to go through some refresher of a concept in probabilities
Dialogue: 0,0:49:07.39,0:49:10.07,Default,,0,0,0,,就是联合概率分布\Nthat is the joint probability distribution.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:11.27,0:49:14.49,Default,,0,0,0,,假设\NSo here, if you suppose that
Dialogue: 0,0:49:14.49,0:49:20.35,Default,,0,0,0,,你有两个依不同分布采样的随机变量\Nyou have two random variables that are drawn from two distributions,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:20.35,0:49:25.04,Default,,0,0,0,,比如x_1和x_2这两个随机变量\Nlet's say it's x_1 and x_2, the random variables,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:25.04,0:49:33.87,Default,,0,0,0,,你可以计算联合概率分布\Nthen, you can compute the joint probability distribution,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:33.87,0:49:39.80,Default,,0,0,0,,方法是取x_1的概率密度\Nby taking the probability density of x_1,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:41.17,0:49:47.39,Default,,0,0,0,,乘以x_2在给定x_1条件下的条件概率\Nand multiplying that by the conditional probability of x_2 given x_1.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:47.39,0:49:51.21,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是定义 就是概率的链式法则\NSo, this is just by definition, it's the probability chain of rule.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:52.40,0:49:59.16,Default,,0,0,0,,在实践中 当你有一个联合概率分布时\NAnd in practice, when you have a joint probability distribution,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:59.16,0:50:02.99,Default,,0,0,0,,联合概率分布的一种表示方式是热力图\None way you can represent that is through a heat map.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:02.99,0:50:08.29,Default,,0,0,0,,这个热力图有两个轴\NSo here, you have, let's say, your two axes.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:08.29,0:50:14.04,Default,,0,0,0,,一个沿x_1方向 另一个沿x_2方向\NOne is representing the one along x_1, and the other one along x_2.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:14.04,0:50:19.09,Default,,0,0,0,,这里你看到的颜色是\NAnd then, here, the color that you see here is
Dialogue: 0,0:50:19.09,0:50:23.53,Default,,0,0,0,,联合概率分布的密度值\Nthe density value of this joint probability distribution.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:26.55,0:50:33.57,Default,,0,0,0,,假设这个区域是[0,1]×[0,1]\NSo, this is, for instance, [0,1]×[0,1].
Dialogue: 0,0:50:33.57,0:50:38.23,Default,,0,0,0,,对于条件概率 你的做法是\NAnd the way you would go about doing this for the conditional probabilities is
Dialogue: 0,0:50:38.23,0:50:41.45,Default,,0,0,0,,只看其中的某一列\Nyou would actually just look at one column.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:43.68,0:50:47.41,Default,,0,0,0,,这里 x_2在给定x_1下的概率\NAnd here the probability of x_2 given x_1 would be
Dialogue: 0,0:50:47.41,0:50:55.08,Default,,0,0,0,,是联合概率分布在这个格子中的值\Nthe proportion of the value of the joint probability distribution in that square
Dialogue: 0,0:50:55.08,0:51:02.63,Default,,0,0,0,,除以给定x_1值下所有格子的总和\Nover the sum of all the squares for that given value x_1, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:02.63,0:51:05.25,Default,,0,0,0,,到目前为止 我只是在复习\NSo, so far, I'm just recapping
Dialogue: 0,0:51:05.25,0:51:10.28,Default,,0,0,0,,我们已知的关于联合概率分布的知识\Nwhat we know about joint probability distributions and conditional probabilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:11.56,0:51:19.57,Default,,0,0,0,,我想告诉你们一个叫做边际化的概念\NSo, what I want to tell you is a notion of what we call marginalization,
Dialogue: 0,0:51:19.57,0:51:28.33,Default,,0,0,0,,即如果你想得到单个随机变量的概率\Nwhich is if you want to obtain the probability of just one random variable,
Dialogue: 0,0:51:28.33,0:51:30.60,Default,,0,0,0,,你可以做的是\Nthen, what you can do is
Dialogue: 0,0:51:30.60,0:51:37.32,Default,,0,0,0,,把单个随机变量和第二个随机变量的联合概率求和\Nto sum the joint probability of that random variable and a second random variable,
Dialogue: 0,0:51:37.32,0:51:41.79,Default,,0,0,0,,沿第二个变量求和\Nand you can sum it along that second variable.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:43.43,0:51:46.37,Default,,0,0,0,,这就叫做边际化\NAnd this is called marginalization.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:46.37,0:51:47.56,Default,,0,0,0,,你们都知道...\NDo you all know...
Dialogue: 0,0:51:47.56,0:51:50.48,Default,,0,0,0,,你们都听说过边际化吗？\NHave you all heard what marginalization is?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:50.48,0:51:51.68,Default,,0,0,0,,听说过？\NYeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:51.68,0:51:52.91,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NOK, cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:52.91,0:51:55.32,Default,,0,0,0,,那我说的就有点显而易见了\NSo, what I'm saying is a little bit obvious then.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:57.29,0:52:04.21,Default,,0,0,0,,在这个图中 你要得到p(x_1)的方式是\NSo, in this figure, so, the way you would obtain p(x_1) is
Dialogue: 0,0:52:04.21,0:52:11.68,Default,,0,0,0,,把x_1对应的所有格子求和 一个接一个\Nyou sum all the squares relative to x_1, again, and again, and again.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:11.68,0:52:17.25,Default,,0,0,0,,这样你就可以重建你的概率分布\NAnd you can reconstitute your probability distribution.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:17.25,0:52:22.07,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是从图形角度来看边际分布的方法\NSo, that's the way you would see this from a graphical perspective.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:23.79,0:52:28.24,Default,,0,0,0,,我们刚才看的是只有两个随机变量的情况\NAnd so, we saw that when we only have two random variables.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:28.24,0:52:34.56,Default,,0,0,0,,但当我们有T个随机变量时 你也可以这么做\NBut you can very well do that when we have T random variables.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:34.56,0:52:41.41,Default,,0,0,0,,幻灯片上方给出的是概率链式法则\NAnd so, here, we have the probability chain rule at the top of the slide.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:41.41,0:52:51.56,Default,,0,0,0,,就是p(x_1)×p(x_2|x_1)×...×p(x_T|x_1,...,x_\{T-1\})\NSo, you have p(x_1)×p(x_2|x_1)×...×p(x_T|x_1,...,x_\{T-1\}).
Dialogue: 0,0:52:51.56,0:52:56.61,Default,,0,0,0,,这里只是把前面的2维情况扩展到T维情况\NSo, this is just extending that to a dimension of T.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:58.52,0:53:05.37,Default,,0,0,0,,有一个你在论文中会经常看到的记法\NAnd one notation that you will see very often in papers is this one.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:05.37,0:53:17.45,Default,,0,0,0,,T个变量的联合概率分布通常记作p(x_\{1:T\})\NSo, the joint probability distribution of T variables is usually denoted p(x_\{1:T\}).
Dialogue: 0,0:53:17.45,0:53:20.48,Default,,0,0,0,,这么写只是为了节省空间\NSo, it is just to save space.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:20.48,0:53:25.69,Default,,0,0,0,,我展示这些幻灯片的原因只是想告诉你们\NAnd the reason why I'm presenting these slides is just to tell you that
Dialogue: 0,0:53:25.69,0:53:29.67,Default,,0,0,0,,这是人们使用的主要记法 以及它的含义\Nthis is the main notation that people use, and this is what it means.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:31.99,0:53:32.59,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NCool.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:32.59,0:53:35.76,Default,,0,0,0,,使用这个简化的记法\NAnd with that simplified notation,
Dialogue: 0,0:53:35.76,0:53:40.41,Default,,0,0,0,,你就可以把之前的公式重写成这页幻灯片的这个样子\Nyou can just rewrite the formulas from before as follows.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:42.13,0:53:42.92,Default,,0,0,0,,现在\NSo now,
Dialogue: 0,0:53:42.92,0:53:51.80,Default,,0,0,0,,如果我们回到之前那个问题 找到参数θ\Nif we were to come back to the problem that we had around finding parameters θ
Dialogue: 0,0:53:51.80,0:53:57.92,Default,,0,0,0,,使得模型看到训练数据的概率最大\Nthat maximize the probability of our models seeing the training data,
Dialogue: 0,0:53:57.92,0:54:05.37,Default,,0,0,0,,这里 我们想做的就是把log(p_θ(x_0))给表示出来\Nhere, what we want to do is to express log(p_θ(x_0)).
Dialogue: 0,0:54:07.29,0:54:10.35,Default,,0,0,0,,我们在前几张幻灯片中已经了解到\NSo, we've seen a few slides ago that
Dialogue: 0,0:54:12.43,0:54:21.52,Default,,0,0,0,,得到x_0的方式是先依时间T的噪声分布采样\Nthe way we obtain x_0 is sampling from a noise distribution at time T,
Dialogue: 0,0:54:21.52,0:54:28.56,Default,,0,0,0,,然后从T到T-1 一步步到0\Nand then, going step by step from T to T-1, etc, up until 0.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:31.07,0:54:38.08,Default,,0,0,0,,为了计算出p_θ 你的一个想法可能是\NSo, in order to compute this quantity, one idea for you could be
Dialogue: 0,0:54:38.08,0:54:45.07,Default,,0,0,0,,取所有时间步上的联合概率分布\Nto take the joint probability distribution over all the time steps,
Dialogue: 0,0:54:45.07,0:54:51.85,Default,,0,0,0,,然后对除x_0以外的所有概率求和\Nand then, sum across all these different quantities except x_0.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:51.85,0:54:56.21,Default,,0,0,0,,也就是你可以做边际化 对吧？\NA.K.A. you can just marginalize, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:54:56.21,0:55:20.73,Default,,0,0,0,,一个想法是log(p_θ(x_0))就是log(∫(p_θ(x_0,x_\{1:T\})dx_\{1:T\}))\NSo, one idea is to say that log(p_θ(x_0)) is log(∫(p_θ(x_0,x_\{1:T\})dx_\{1:T\})).
Dialogue: 0,0:55:22.12,0:55:25.79,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是边际化的定义\NSo, this is just the definition of marginalizing.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:27.69,0:55:31.20,Default,,0,0,0,,这个公式的问题是\NSo, the problem with this formulation is that
Dialogue: 0,0:55:31.20,0:55:34.08,Default,,0,0,0,,我们实际上无法计算这个公式\Nit's actually something we cannot compute,
Dialogue: 0,0:55:34.08,0:55:39.21,Default,,0,0,0,,因为这里我们说的是要边际化...\Nbecause here, we're saying let's marginalize...
Dialogue: 0,0:55:39.21,0:55:46.25,Default,,0,0,0,,我们要对从加噪图像到清晰图像的所有可能轨迹求和\NLet's sum across all possible trajectories from noise to clean image.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:46.25,0:55:49.47,Default,,0,0,0,,问题是有非常多这样的轨迹\NSo, the problem is there are many of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:49.47,0:55:57.32,Default,,0,0,0,,而这些x是向量 这个向量的长度可以非常大\NAnd these x's, we saw that these are vectors, and they can be pretty big.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:57.32,0:56:02.85,Default,,0,0,0,,长话短说 这个公式在实践中是无法计算的\NSo, long story short is this is in practice something that we cannot compute,
Dialogue: 0,0:56:05.00,0:56:06.29,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是为什么\Nwhich is the reason
Dialogue: 0,0:56:06.29,0:56:13.57,Default,,0,0,0,,我们要用接下来33分钟讲一个方法\Nwhy we have a recipe that we will go through in the next 33 minutes as to
Dialogue: 0,0:56:13.57,0:56:19.51,Default,,0,0,0,,这个方法是如何用我们定义的前向过程来计算这个公式\Nhow we can compute that using the forward process that we have defined.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:21.36,0:56:23.40,Default,,0,0,0,,为了节省时间\NSo, in the interest of time,
Dialogue: 0,0:56:23.40,0:56:26.87,Default,,0,0,0,,我会跳过一些黑板推导 跳过这些推导不会带来什么影响\NI'm going to skip some blackboard derivation, which is fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:26.87,0:56:28.99,Default,,0,0,0,,我直接告诉你们这个技巧\NI'm just going to give you the trick.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:28.99,0:56:32.03,Default,,0,0,0,,如果时间允许 我们可以做几个推导\NIf time permits, we can do a few ones.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:32.03,0:56:34.65,Default,,0,0,0,,但对你们来说重要的是\NBut the important thing for you is
Dialogue: 0,0:56:34.65,0:56:40.76,Default,,0,0,0,,从宏观层面理解损失函数的推导策略\Nto just understand the high-level strategy around obtaining the loss
Dialogue: 0,0:56:40.76,0:56:42.69,Default,,0,0,0,,我们将用推导出来的损失函数训练我们的模型\Nthat will be used to train our model.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:45.25,0:56:46.41,Default,,0,0,0,,没问题吧？\NSounds good?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:48.57,0:56:49.19,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NCool.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:49.19,0:56:51.32,Default,,0,0,0,,我们从第一步开始\NSo, let's start with the first step.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:52.76,0:56:55.40,Default,,0,0,0,,我之前告诉过你们\NSo, I told you that
Dialogue: 0,0:56:55.40,0:57:01.76,Default,,0,0,0,,我们实际上无法计算这个表达式\Nthis expression is something that is actually not something we can compute,
Dialogue: 0,0:57:01.76,0:57:04.40,Default,,0,0,0,,因为这个表达式不可处理\Nbecause it's just intractable.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:04.40,0:57:08.92,Default,,0,0,0,,所以 一个常用的技巧是\NSo, a common trick that people use is
Dialogue: 0,0:57:08.92,0:57:13.44,Default,,0,0,0,,找到一个容易计算的表达式\Nto find something that is easy to compute
Dialogue: 0,0:57:13.44,0:57:17.03,Default,,0,0,0,,这个表达式计算的不一定是我们关心的那个量\Nthat is not necessarily the quantity of interest,
Dialogue: 0,0:57:17.03,0:57:22.85,Default,,0,0,0,,但也许可以是一个接近你想要的量的某个界\Nbut maybe a bound that is close to what you want.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:22.85,0:57:27.13,Default,,0,0,0,,这里 你想要最大化那个表达式\NSo here, what you want is to maximize that expression.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:27.13,0:57:31.76,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你去最大化一个你知道比它小的表达式\NSo, if you were to maximize something that you know is lower than that,
Dialogue: 0,0:57:31.76,0:57:33.55,Default,,0,0,0,,也就是最大化一个下界\Nso, a lower bound,
Dialogue: 0,0:57:33.55,0:57:36.72,Default,,0,0,0,,那这个下界也能让你有一定的信心\Nthen it would also allow you to gain some confidence that
Dialogue: 0,0:57:36.72,0:57:38.53,Default,,0,0,0,,认为你在最大化正确的量\Nyou're maximizing the right thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:40.44,0:57:44.45,Default,,0,0,0,,幻灯片上有一个看起来很吓人的公式\NSo, there is a very scary formula on the slides,
Dialogue: 0,0:57:44.45,0:57:48.49,Default,,0,0,0,,我们现在就要来研究一下这个公式 这就是ELBO\Nwhich we'll go through right now, which is the ELBO.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:48.49,0:57:51.53,Default,,0,0,0,,在上这门课之前 有人听说过ELBO吗？\NHave you heard of the ELBO before this class?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:51.53,0:57:52.40,Default,,0,0,0,,听说过？\NYeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:52.40,0:57:55.45,Default,,0,0,0,,ELBO的全称是证据下界\NELBO stands for Evidence Lower BOund.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:55.45,0:58:01.00,Default,,0,0,0,,它的意思是 这是一个量的表达式\NAnd what that means is it's an expression of a quantity
Dialogue: 0,0:58:01.00,0:58:04.61,Default,,0,0,0,,而这个量是我们关心的那个量的下界\Nthat is a lower bound of the quantity that we care about.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:06.60,0:58:10.21,Default,,0,0,0,,ELBO很重要 所以我打算推导一下\NAnd actually, this is quite important, so I think I will derive it.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:13.77,0:58:17.31,Default,,0,0,0,,在我擦黑板的同时\NSo, while I'm cleaning the blackboards,
Dialogue: 0,0:58:17.31,0:58:22.03,Default,,0,0,0,,我先告诉你们这里的技巧是什么\NI just want to tell you about what the trick is.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:22.03,0:58:31.47,Default,,0,0,0,,技巧是 我们有已经定义好的前向过程 也就是q\NThe trick is that we have our forward process that we have defined, so, q.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:31.47,0:58:40.09,Default,,0,0,0,,我们想让q以某种方式出现在我们的表达式中\NAnd what we want to do is to have q be in some way something that we appear.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:40.09,0:58:46.85,Default,,0,0,0,,我们想在表达式中引入q\NLike in our equation, we want to involve q in some way,
Dialogue: 0,0:58:46.85,0:58:51.84,Default,,0,0,0,,因为q就是我们定义好的前向过程\Nbecause what q is, q is this forward process that we have defined.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:51.84,0:58:57.01,Default,,0,0,0,,是我们设定的噪声调度 是我们设定的β_t、α_t 我们知道q是什么\NWhen we do the noise schedule, this β_t, α_t, we know that.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:57.88,0:59:02.87,Default,,0,0,0,,所以 我们想做的是把这个公式表示为q的函数\NSo, what we want to do is to express that as a function of q.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:04.93,0:59:10.19,Default,,0,0,0,,我们回到log(p_θ(x_0))\NSo, we go back with the log(p_θ(x_0)),
Dialogue: 0,0:59:11.47,0:59:17.64,Default,,0,0,0,,我前面已经提到过 我们想尝试计算它在x_1到x_T上的边际概率\Nwhich we said we tried to marginalize across x_1 to x_T.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:17.64,0:59:20.16,Default,,0,0,0,,因此 我这里只是再写一遍上面的公式\NSo, I'm just going to rewrite what we had above.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:28.87,0:59:34.87,Default,,0,0,0,,正如我前面提到的 我要让q出现在公式里\NAnd then, what I'm going to do, as I mentioned, is have q appear.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:34.87,0:59:37.73,Default,,0,0,0,,我们要用一个非常常用的技巧\NSo, very common trick.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:37.73,0:59:40.20,Default,,0,0,0,,我要做的是\NWhat I'm going to do is
Dialogue: 0,0:59:40.20,0:59:45.29,Default,,0,0,0,,把分子和分母同时乘以想要出现的那个量\Nto multiply the numerator and the denominator by that quantity.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:45.29,0:59:55.33,Default,,0,0,0,,因此 我要用这一项乘以q...\NSo, I'm going to do this one times q of...
Dialogue: 0,0:59:55.33,1:00:01.36,Default,,0,0,0,,给定一张清晰图像 由q给出的轨迹是什么\NSo, given a clean image, what is the trajectory that is given by q
Dialogue: 0,1:00:01.36,1:00:06.92,Default,,0,0,0,,轨迹是q(x_\{1:T\}|x_0)\NSo, it's q(x_\{1:T\}|x_0).
Dialogue: 0,1:00:21.89,1:00:24.36,Default,,0,0,0,,到目前为止大家都能跟上吗？\NOK, everyone is following me so far?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:24.36,1:00:27.29,Default,,0,0,0,,这是一个很常规的技巧\NJust a very regular trick.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:27.29,1:00:29.55,Default,,0,0,0,,从这里我们怎么继续往下推导？\NSo, OK, so where do we go from there?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:30.93,1:00:34.23,Default,,0,0,0,,我暂时把log去掉\NSo, I'm just going to remove the log for now.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:34.23,1:00:35.83,Default,,0,0,0,,这个等式是成立的\NSo, this is true.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:37.13,1:00:46.51,Default,,0,0,0,,这个表达式实际上就是积分号内部的量的期望\NSo, this expression is actually nothing else than the expectation of this quantity,
Dialogue: 0,1:00:49.21,1:00:57.33,Default,,0,0,0,,因为这个表达式的意思是你依这个分布采样x_\{1:T\}\Nbecause this is as if you were sampling x_\{1:T\} from this distribution.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:57.33,1:01:01.93,Default,,0,0,0,,也就是说 你可以写成这样\NSo, it's as if you were writing this, right?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:14.84,1:01:20.25,Default,,0,0,0,,也就是说 它是这个比值的期望\NSo, it's as if you were saying it's the expectation of this ratio,
Dialogue: 0,1:01:20.25,1:01:27.51,Default,,0,0,0,,即p_θ(x_\{0:T\})/q(x_\{1:T\}|x_0)的期望\Nwhich is p_θ(x_\{0:T\})/q(x_\{1:T\}|x_0),
Dialogue: 0,1:01:28.87,1:01:42.41,Default,,0,0,0,,其中x_\{1:T\}是依q(x_\{1:T\}|x_0)采样得到的\Nwhere x_\{1:T\} is something that you draw from q(x_\{1:T\}|x_0).
Dialogue: 0,1:01:45.40,1:01:46.93,Default,,0,0,0,,我希望...\NOK, I hope...
Dialogue: 0,1:01:46.93,1:01:50.01,Default,,0,0,0,,顺便说一下 不用担心 所有内容都会在录像里\NSo, don't worry by the way. It's all going to be in the recording.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:50.01,1:01:53.93,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你看不清我写的内容 那可以看录像 看录像会更清楚\NIt's going to be much clearer in case you cannot see very clear what I'm writing.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:53.93,1:01:56.11,Default,,0,0,0,,但我写的是这个期望\NBut what I'm writing is the expectation.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:56.11,1:01:57.65,Default,,0,0,0,,这个量是\NThis quantity is
Dialogue: 0,1:01:57.65,1:02:06.99,Default,,0,0,0,,p_θ(x_\{0:T\})/q(x_\{1:T\}|x_0)这个比值的期望\Nthe expectation of the ratio between p_θ(x_\{0:T\})/q(x_\{1:T\}|x_0)
Dialogue: 0,1:02:06.99,1:02:15.48,Default,,0,0,0,,这是依我们已知的前向过程采样轨迹1:T得到x_\{1:T\}的期望\Nby sampling x_\{1:T\}, so, the trajectory 1:T via the forward process that we know,
Dialogue: 0,1:02:15.48,1:02:19.15,Default,,0,0,0,,采样由x_\{1:T\}|x_0给出\Nwhich is given by x_\{1:T\}|x_0.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:20.57,1:02:21.71,Default,,0,0,0,,没问题吧？\NOK?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:23.48,1:02:27.07,Default,,0,0,0,,从这里我们怎么继续往下推导？\NSo, where do we go from here?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:27.07,1:02:32.24,Default,,0,0,0,,这里要用到一个非常常用的技巧\NSo, it turns out that there is a very common trick.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:36.19,1:02:41.08,Default,,0,0,0,,这个技巧叫做Jensen不等式\NVery common trick out there that's called the Jensen inequality,
Dialogue: 0,1:02:41.08,1:02:45.37,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你有一个凸函数或凹函数\Nwhere if you have a convex or concave function,
Dialogue: 0,1:02:45.37,1:02:50.19,Default,,0,0,0,,那么我们接下来就会看到 你会有一个非常好的性质\Nyou have some very nice property about something we're going to see.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:50.19,1:02:56.15,Default,,0,0,0,,具体来说 在这种情况下 log是凹函数\NAnd in particular, in this case, log is a concave function.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:57.51,1:03:03.32,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你有某个期望的log\NSo, if you have the log of some expectation,
Dialogue: 0,1:03:03.32,1:03:18.97,Default,,0,0,0,,那么这个期望的log实际上大于等于log的期望\Nit's actually something that is greater or equal than the expectation of the log.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:18.97,1:03:22.80,Default,,0,0,0,,我不打算把整个东西都写出来 但你们知道我的意思是什么\NI'm not going to write this whole thing, but you know what I mean.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:24.95,1:03:26.89,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是Jensen不等式\NSo, this is Jensen's inequality.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:28.76,1:03:30.68,Default,,0,0,0,,拼写是 J-E-N-S-E-N\NJ-E-N-S-E-N.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:33.33,1:03:36.17,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是幻灯片上给出的这个公式\NAnd this is exactly what we get here.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:38.71,1:03:48.15,Default,,0,0,0,,我们往下推导的思想是 不再对所有可能的轨迹求和\NSo, one way we progressed is instead of summing through all possible trajectories,
Dialogue: 0,1:03:48.15,1:03:53.05,Default,,0,0,0,,现在我们实际上是依轨迹采样\Nnow what we're doing is we're actually sampling from trajectories
Dialogue: 0,1:03:53.05,1:03:58.53,Default,,0,0,0,,依我们已知的前向过程采样\Nthat were drawing from the forward process, which we know.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:00.88,1:04:06.88,Default,,0,0,0,,你可能会疑惑 为什么幻灯片上采样的是x_\{0:T\}\NAnd now, you're wondering why in the slide are we sampling x_\{0:T\},
Dialogue: 0,1:04:06.88,1:04:13.04,Default,,0,0,0,,而我说要依q(x_\{1:T\}|x_0)采样得到x_\{1:T\}\Nbut here I said x_\{1:T\} sample from q(x_\{1:T\}|x_0).
Dialogue: 0,1:04:13.04,1:04:17.08,Default,,0,0,0,,这是因为 如果你对整个x_\{0:T\}取期望\NIt is because if you take the expectation of this whole thing,
Dialogue: 0,1:04:19.39,1:04:28.49,Default,,0,0,0,,你就是对x_0取期望 再乘以对x_\{1:T\}取期望\Nthen, you take the expectation over x_0 of expectation of x_\{1:T\} times that.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:28.49,1:04:34.31,Default,,0,0,0,,你用到了我们刚看过的概率链式法则\NSo, you use the chain rule of probability that we saw right before.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:34.31,1:04:38.03,Default,,0,0,0,,这样取期望\NAnd it's exactly the same as just one expectation of
Dialogue: 0,1:04:38.03,1:04:45.36,Default,,0,0,0,,和通过q(x_\{0:T\})采样整个联合概率分布取期望 两者完全一样\Nsampling the whole joint probability distribution through this q(x_\{0:T\}).
Dialogue: 0,1:04:47.91,1:04:49.31,Default,,0,0,0,,大家能理解吗？\NDoes this make sense?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:51.04,1:04:55.40,Default,,0,0,0,,你看到这个公式后可能会想\NSo, you may see this formula and wonder,
Dialogue: 0,1:04:55.40,1:05:00.23,Default,,0,0,0,,这个公式仍然超级复杂 该怎么计算呢？\NOK, it's still super complicated, how can I compute that?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:00.23,1:05:04.79,Default,,0,0,0,,现在你还不知道这个公式是可处理的 我只是告诉你这个公式是可处理的\NWell, right now, you do not know that it is tractable. I'm just telling you.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:04.79,1:05:11.01,Default,,0,0,0,,但这里的直觉是 我们并不是对所有可能的轨迹求和\NBut the intuition here is we're actually not summing through all possible trajectories.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:11.01,1:05:14.79,Default,,0,0,0,,我们实际上要求和的轨迹\NWe're actually summing through trajectories
Dialogue: 0,1:05:14.79,1:05:18.01,Default,,0,0,0,,是依前向过程采样得到的\Nthat we're sampling from the forward process.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:21.24,1:05:22.28,Default,,0,0,0,,对吧？\NYeah?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:23.29,1:05:25.44,Default,,0,0,0,,这是ELBO的第1步\NSo now, it's step number 1.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:25.44,1:05:32.73,Default,,0,0,0,,ELBO的第2步是证明这个表达式是可以计算的\NStep number 2 is proving or showing that this is something that you can compute.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:34.09,1:05:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,但在此之前\NBut before that,
Dialogue: 0,1:05:35.00,1:05:40.63,Default,,0,0,0,,我还需要带大家复习一个非常重要的概念\NI'm going to, again, give you some refresher of a very important concept,
Dialogue: 0,1:05:40.63,1:05:43.83,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是KL散度\Nthat is the KL divergence.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:44.87,1:05:48.16,Default,,0,0,0,,谁听说过KL散度？\NWho has heard of KL divergence?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:48.16,1:05:49.81,Default,,0,0,0,,都听说过？好的\NYeah, everyone? OK.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:49.81,1:05:52.51,Default,,0,0,0,,我来带大家回忆一下什么是KL散度\NI'm just going to remind you what KL divergence is.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:52.51,1:05:57.72,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你取两个概率分布 比如P和Q\NSo, if you take two probability distributions, so, let's say P and Q,
Dialogue: 0,1:05:57.72,1:06:02.48,Default,,0,0,0,,你想衡量这两个分布之间有多远\Nand you want to measure how far apart they are,
Dialogue: 0,1:06:02.48,1:06:08.21,Default,,0,0,0,,有一个算子叫做KL散度\Nthen, there is some operator that is here the KL divergence,
Dialogue: 0,1:06:08.21,1:06:12.16,Default,,0,0,0,,KL散度可以量化两个概率分布之间的距离\Nwhich quantifies how far apart they are.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:14.20,1:06:26.80,Default,,0,0,0,,KL散度的做法是取...\NAnd the way they do that is by taking...
Dialogue: 0,1:06:26.80,1:06:30.01,Default,,0,0,0,,好像幻灯片上有公式和演示 那我沿着幻灯片的内容讲\NMaybe it's something I treat on the slide. So, I'm just going to continue there.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:30.01,1:06:37.15,Default,,0,0,0,,取这两个概率之间比值的log的和\NSo, by taking the sum of the log of the ratio between these two probabilities
Dialogue: 0,1:06:37.15,1:06:42.37,Default,,0,0,0,,同时用概率分布P来加权\Nweighted by the probability distribution P.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:42.37,1:06:46.64,Default,,0,0,0,,在离散情况下 KL散度的表达式如幻灯片所示\NSo, in the discrete world, it's going to be like this.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:46.64,1:06:48.96,Default,,0,0,0,,但我们主要考虑的是连续空间\NBut we're going to be mostly in the continuous world.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:48.96,1:06:55.88,Default,,0,0,0,,在连续空间中 KL散度是这个表达式 要用积分形式\NAnd in the continuous world, the KL divergence is this, but in integral form.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:55.88,1:07:03.55,Default,,0,0,0,,这等价于取比值的对数的期望\NAnd it's the same as saying you take the expectation of the logarithm of the ratio
Dialogue: 0,1:07:03.55,1:07:07.48,Default,,0,0,0,,其中我们假设x是依P采样得到的\Nif you were to assume that x is sampled through P.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:11.60,1:07:12.71,Default,,0,0,0,,没问题吧？\NYeah?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:12.71,1:07:20.75,Default,,0,0,0,,有了这个 我们就可以证明ELBO项...\NOK, so, given that, we can prove that the ELBO term that we saw...
Dialogue: 0,1:07:20.75,1:07:24.99,Default,,0,0,0,,你们知道这个下界\NSo, you know this lower bounds here.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:24.99,1:07:30.87,Default,,0,0,0,,它实际上可以用一些项来表示...\NIt can actually be expressed with terms...
Dialogue: 0,1:07:30.87,1:07:34.97,Default,,0,0,0,,后面的一些项我们不太关心 直接忽略掉\NSo, some terms that we actually don't really care, and we're just going to ignore.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:36.53,1:07:37.97,Default,,0,0,0,,再加上这个项\NPlus a term here,
Dialogue: 0,1:07:37.97,1:07:50.23,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是KL散度项 其中第一个分布是q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0)\Nwhich is the KL divergence of q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0), so, it's the first distribution,
Dialogue: 0,1:07:50.23,1:07:52.53,Default,,0,0,0,,第二个分布是\Nand the second distribution is
Dialogue: 0,1:07:52.53,1:08:01.84,Default,,0,0,0,,实际上就是噪声较少的图像x_\{t-1\}|x_t的概率\Nactually, the probability of having the less noisy image x_\{t-1\}|x_t,
Dialogue: 0,1:08:01.84,1:08:04.00,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是我们想要学习的东西\Nwhich is the thing that we want to learn.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:05.83,1:08:10.11,Default,,0,0,0,,我们没有时间完整推导\NSo, we don't have time to derive this,
Dialogue: 0,1:08:10.11,1:08:15.21,Default,,0,0,0,,但这个推导其实并不复杂\Nbut it's actually not that complicated of a derivation.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:15.21,1:08:18.96,Default,,0,0,0,,你只需要取期望的log\NYou would just take this expectation of log,
Dialogue: 0,1:08:18.96,1:08:22.80,Default,,0,0,0,,然后做一些代数变形\Nand then, you would do some manipulation here and there,
Dialogue: 0,1:08:22.80,1:08:26.85,Default,,0,0,0,,基本上就能把KL散度算子从中提取出来\Nand you can basically pop up the KL divergence operator through that.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:28.99,1:08:34.85,Default,,0,0,0,,我需要你们相信我 ELBO等于幻灯片给出的这个公式\NOK, so, I think this one, I will need you to trust me that this is equal to this.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:34.85,1:08:37.48,Default,,0,0,0,,为什么我们现在很开心？\NSo, why are we happy?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:37.48,1:08:42.77,Default,,0,0,0,,我们开心的原因是\NThe reason why we're happy is because
Dialogue: 0,1:08:42.77,1:08:48.48,Default,,0,0,0,,我们得到了一个很清晰的公式 我们就是在比较两个概率分布\Nwe have a clear comparison between two probability distributions,
Dialogue: 0,1:08:48.48,1:08:53.60,Default,,0,0,0,,一个是我们关心的概率分布 另一个可能是可处理的概率分布\None that we care about, and another one that is potentially something that is tractable.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:55.99,1:09:02.05,Default,,0,0,0,,让我告诉你们q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0)是什么意思\NAnd so, just to tell you what q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0) means.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:02.05,1:09:11.08,Default,,0,0,0,,它的意思是 如果我给你一张带噪图像和一张清晰图像\NSo, it means that if I were to give you a noisy image and a clean image,
Dialogue: 0,1:09:11.08,1:09:13.55,Default,,0,0,0,,我问你的问题是\Nmy question for you would be,
Dialogue: 0,1:09:13.55,1:09:18.20,Default,,0,0,0,,如果我给你这些信息 那么噪声较少的图像会是什么\Nwhat would be the less noisy image if I were to give you this tool.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:20.23,1:09:25.16,Default,,0,0,0,,好消息是 在训练时你知道x_0\NSo, the good thing is that at training time, you know x_0.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:25.16,1:09:27.91,Default,,0,0,0,,所以你可以计算这个量\NSo, you can compute this quantity.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:30.48,1:09:36.49,Default,,0,0,0,,很自然 下一步就是证明\NSo, a natural step for us is now to show that
Dialogue: 0,1:09:36.49,1:09:39.41,Default,,0,0,0,,这里的q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0)确实是可处理的\Nthis quantity that I mentioned is indeed tractable.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:41.23,1:09:48.48,Default,,0,0,0,,我们来看看q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0)到底是什么\NSo, we're going to see what q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0) is.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:50.43,1:09:55.71,Default,,0,0,0,,同样 q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0)就是在问\NSo again, it is the fact of wondering
Dialogue: 0,1:09:55.71,1:09:59.51,Default,,0,0,0,,如果我不仅给你噪声较多的图像 还给你清晰图像\Nwhat is the distribution of the less noisy image
Dialogue: 0,1:09:59.51,1:10:04.63,Default,,0,0,0,,那噪声较少的图像的分布是什么\Nif I were to not only give you the more noisy image, but also the clean image,
Dialogue: 0,1:10:04.63,1:10:07.52,Default,,0,0,0,,我们给出的信息实际上非常多\Nwhich is actually a lot of information.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:09.44,1:10:15.17,Default,,0,0,0,,你可能记得或听说过Bayes规则\NSo, you may remember, or you may have heard of Bayes' rule.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:15.17,1:10:17.88,Default,,0,0,0,,这是我们在这里要用的一个技巧\NAnd it is something that we will use, a trick we will use here.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:19.05,1:10:28.49,Default,,0,0,0,,这里我要用你通常会看到和听到的符号\NSo, using the notations that you would commonly see and read and hear out there,
Dialogue: 0,1:10:28.49,1:10:32.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Bayes规则指的是\Nit's the fact of saying that the posterior
Dialogue: 0,1:10:32.28,1:10:38.67,Default,,0,0,0,,后验等于似然乘以先验再除以边际似然\Nis equal to the likelihood times the prior over the marginal likelihood.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:38.67,1:10:46.55,Default,,0,0,0,,即p(A|B)=p(B|A)p(A)/p(B)\NSo, in this case, it's p(A|B)=p(B|A)p(A)/p(B).
Dialogue: 0,1:10:48.95,1:10:56.08,Default,,0,0,0,,知道Bayes规则 就可以很容易证明q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0)是可处理的\NAnd so, knowing that, it's actually quite easy to show that this thing is tractable.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:56.08,1:10:58.92,Default,,0,0,0,,我们可能需要推导一下\NSo, this is probably something we will derive.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:03.63,1:11:05.35,Default,,0,0,0,,这里...\NSo here...
Dialogue: 0,1:11:10.85,1:11:21.64,Default,,0,0,0,,我们想要的是q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0)\NSo, what we want is q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0).
Dialogue: 0,1:11:23.49,1:11:38.19,Default,,0,0,0,,如果我们用q(·|x_0)的Bayes规则 我们就可以得到...\NSo, if we were to use Bayes' rule with q(·|x_0), so, if you have this formula...
Dialogue: 0,1:11:39.93,1:11:50.81,Default,,0,0,0,,如果把p=q(·|x_0)代入 我们就可以得到...\NSo, if we were to write this by considering p=q(·|x_0), what we would do is...
Dialogue: 0,1:11:50.81,1:11:53.47,Default,,0,0,0,,我所做的就是在应用Bayes规则\NSo, what I'm doing is just applying Bayes' rule.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:54.47,1:12:20.89,Default,,0,0,0,,这个公式等于q(x_t|x_\{t-1\},x_0)q(x_\{t-1\}|x_0)/q(x_t|x_0)\NSo, it's equal to q(x_t|x_\{t-1\},x_0)q(x_\{t-1\}|x_0)/q(x_t|x_0).
Dialogue: 0,1:12:23.52,1:12:27.15,Default,,0,0,0,,大家同意吗？我只是在用Bayes规则\NYou all agree? I'm just doing Bayes' rule.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:27.15,1:12:32.27,Default,,0,0,0,,还有一个我没告诉大家的事情\NSo, it's something that I have not told you so far.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:32.27,1:12:40.96,Default,,0,0,0,,这里的q有一个非常特殊的性质 q满足Markov性\NBut q has a very special property, q is Markovian.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:40.96,1:12:42.71,Default,,0,0,0,,这意味着什么？\NSo, what does that mean?
Dialogue: 0,1:12:43.91,1:13:01.04,Default,,0,0,0,,这意味着q(x_t|x_\{0:T\})实际上等于q(x_t|x_\{t-1\})\NIt means that q(x_t|x_\{0:T\}) is actually equal to q(x_t|x_\{t-1\}).
Dialogue: 0,1:13:01.04,1:13:01.85,Default,,0,0,0,,换句话说\NIn other words,
Dialogue: 0,1:13:01.85,1:13:08.37,Default,,0,0,0,,你只需要知道前一步骤就能知道当前步骤\Nyou only need to know about the previous step to know the current step.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:08.37,1:13:11.05,Default,,0,0,0,,这就叫Markov过程\NSo, it's called a Markov process.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:12.80,1:13:16.83,Default,,0,0,0,,所以 这个公式可以简化为q(x_t|x_\{t-1\},x_0)\NSo, this simplifies to q(x_t|x_\{t-1\},x_0).
Dialogue: 0,1:13:18.67,1:13:20.59,Default,,0,0,0,,我们之前已经看到\NAnd then, we saw before that
Dialogue: 0,1:13:20.59,1:13:30.41,Default,,0,0,0,,q(x_\{t-1\}|x_0)和q(x_t|x_0)都是可处理的量\Nq(x_\{t-1\}|x_0) and q(x_t|x_0) are quantities that are tractable.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:30.41,1:13:32.17,Default,,0,0,0,,这两个量都是正态分布\NThey are this normal distribution.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:32.17,1:13:34.27,Default,,0,0,0,,大家还记得我前面给出的推导吧\NDo you remember this derivation I made with,
Dialogue: 0,1:13:34.27,1:13:40.31,Default,,0,0,0,,就是把x_\{t-1\}的函数替换成x_\{t-2\}的函数 一直替换成x_0的函数\NOK, let's replace x_\{t-1\} as a function of x_\{t-2\} until getting x_0?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:40.31,1:13:41.84,Default,,0,0,0,,还记得吗？\NDo you remember?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:41.84,1:13:45.33,Default,,0,0,0,,所以 这两个量是可处理的\NSo, these two quantities, they are tractable.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:45.33,1:13:48.68,Default,,0,0,0,,这个量是可处理的 这个量也是可处理的\NThis is tractable, this is tractable.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:48.68,1:13:51.71,Default,,0,0,0,,实际上 我们不太关心q(x_t|x_0)这一项\NActually, this one, we don't really care,
Dialogue: 0,1:13:51.71,1:13:58.83,Default,,0,0,0,,因为我们想计算的是q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0)\Nbecause we want to compute q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0),
Dialogue: 0,1:13:58.83,1:14:07.33,Default,,0,0,0,,因此 这里我们只改变x_\{t-1\} 而q(x_t|x_0)这一项是固定的\Nso here, we're only varying x_\{t-1\}, but q(x_t|x_0), everything is fixed.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:07.33,1:14:10.32,Default,,0,0,0,,你可以把q(x_t|x_0)理解为一个常数\NSo, you can interpret that as a constant.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:12.12,1:14:13.28,Default,,0,0,0,,没问题吧？\NYeah?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:14.72,1:14:17.31,Default,,0,0,0,,我们最后得到的是...\NAnd so, what we end up with...
Dialogue: 0,1:14:17.31,1:14:19.32,Default,,0,0,0,,我还不能把黑板上的这块内容遮住\NI cannot do that.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:20.99,1:14:22.16,Default,,0,0,0,,请问？\NYeah?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:27.16,1:14:29.65,Default,,0,0,0,,你是指这一项吗？\NAre you referring to this one?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:29.65,1:14:31.31,Default,,0,0,0,,左侧这一项\NThe left-hand side.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:34.65,1:14:35.91,Default,,0,0,0,,原因是…\NSo…
Dialogue: 0,1:14:37.31,1:14:40.49,Default,,0,0,0,,原因是这样的\NSo, here's the thing.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:40.49,1:14:49.60,Default,,0,0,0,,在这个推导中 我们真正关心的量是q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0)\NIn this derivation, the quantity that we actually care about is q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0).
Dialogue: 0,1:14:51.92,1:14:59.45,Default,,0,0,0,,这只是因为我们从ELBO出发进行推导 最终得到的就是这个公式\NSo, this is just because of the derivation of the ELBO, the fact that we end up here.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:59.45,1:15:03.31,Default,,0,0,0,,是的 这就是我们感兴趣的分布\NYeah, and that's just the fact that we just are interested in
Dialogue: 0,1:15:03.31,1:15:05.96,Default,,0,0,0,,当我们知道噪声较多的图像和清晰图像时\Nwhat is the distribution of the less noisy data
Dialogue: 0,1:15:05.96,1:15:09.89,Default,,0,0,0,,噪声较少的图像的分布是什么\Nif we what the noisier one is and the clean image is.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:09.89,1:15:11.87,Default,,0,0,0,,这是我们关心的分布\NThat's the thing that we care about.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:14.73,1:15:23.88,Default,,0,0,0,,这里 我想说的是 q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0)是...\NAnd so here, what I want to say is that this is something...
Dialogue: 0,1:15:24.88,1:15:50.92,Default,,0,0,0,,即q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0)与q(x_t|x_\{t-1\})q(x_\{t-1\}|x_0)成比例\NSo, q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0) is proportional of q(x_t|x_\{t-1\})q(x_\{t-1\}|x_0).
Dialogue: 0,1:15:52.89,1:15:56.95,Default,,0,0,0,,这是个高斯分布 这也是个高斯分布\NThis is Gaussian. This is Gaussian.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:58.29,1:16:03.32,Default,,0,0,0,,两个高斯分布概率的乘积仍为高斯分布\NThe product of probabilities of Gaussian is a Gaussian.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:05.24,1:16:07.19,Default,,0,0,0,,我不打算推导所有细节\NI'm not going to derive everything,
Dialogue: 0,1:16:07.19,1:16:15.64,Default,,0,0,0,,但请相信 q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0)的形式是正态分布\Nbut please trust me that the form of q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0) is a normal distribution,
Dialogue: 0,1:16:15.64,1:16:19.87,Default,,0,0,0,,具体来说 这个正态分布的均值就是这个公式\Nin particular, with the mean of this formula.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:19.87,1:16:22.65,Default,,0,0,0,,我不会把这个公式念出来\NI'm not going to read it, but it's a function of
Dialogue: 0,1:16:22.65,1:16:29.83,Default,,0,0,0,,但这个公式是带噪图像 以及从x_0到x_t所用噪声的函数\Nthe noisy image, and then, the sampled noise that allows you to go from x_0 to x_t.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:32.97,1:16:34.20,Default,,0,0,0,,没问题吧？\NOK?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:34.20,1:16:42.52,Default,,0,0,0,,这个分布是精确的 我们没有引入任何近似过程\NSo, this distribution is exact, meaning we have not approximated anything.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:42.52,1:16:47.97,Default,,0,0,0,,我们也完全知道这个分布是什么 因为是我们自己定义的前向过程\NAnd this is something that we know, because we have defined our forward process.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:47.97,1:16:50.55,Default,,0,0,0,,这里我们有点作弊 因为我们在说\NAnd here, we're cheating a little bit, because we're saying,
Dialogue: 0,1:16:50.55,1:16:53.28,Default,,0,0,0,,如果我给你噪声较多的图像 同时也给你清晰图像\Nwhat is the less noisy distribution
Dialogue: 0,1:16:53.28,1:16:57.32,Default,,0,0,0,,那么噪声较少的图像的分布是什么\Nif I give you the more noisy one, but also the clean image.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:57.32,1:17:00.93,Default,,0,0,0,,这有点作弊 因为训练时我们知道x_0是什么\NSo, it's a little bit of cheating, because at training time, we know what x_0 is.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:02.27,1:17:05.11,Default,,0,0,0,,当然 推理时我们不知道\NOf course, at inference time, we do not.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:06.24,1:17:09.91,Default,,0,0,0,,好 我们知道了其中一项是可处理的\NSo, OK, so, we know one term.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:11.29,1:17:16.09,Default,,0,0,0,,第二项是p_θ(x_\{t-1\}|x_t)\NThe second term is this p_θ(x_\{t-1\}|x_t).
Dialogue: 0,1:17:16.09,1:17:18.55,Default,,0,0,0,,现在来证明这一项也是可处理的\NNow, let's show that it is tractable.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:18.55,1:17:23.51,Default,,0,0,0,,这个证明很容易 因为我们可以选择p_θ是什么\NWell, that one is going to be easy, because we can choose what p_θ is.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:24.84,1:17:32.27,Default,,0,0,0,,假设p_θ也是高斯分布是非常合理的\NAnd it turns out that it's very fair for us to assume that it is also a Gaussian,
Dialogue: 0,1:17:32.27,1:17:39.95,Default,,0,0,0,,因为x_\{t-1\}|x_t的前向过程也近似是高斯分布\Njust because the forward process of x_\{t-1\}|x_t is also approximately a Gaussian.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:41.27,1:17:45.65,Default,,0,0,0,,具体的论证过程会稍微深入一些\NSo, justification for that is a little bit more into the weeds.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:45.65,1:17:47.29,Default,,0,0,0,,所以我这里就不展开了\NSo, I'm not going to go into that.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:47.29,1:17:55.87,Default,,0,0,0,,总而言之 在这部分 我们就是假设\NBut all of that to say that in this part, we're just making the assumption that
Dialogue: 0,1:17:57.04,1:17:59.61,Default,,0,0,0,,我们想要学习的是一个高斯分布\Nwhat we want to learn is a Gaussian.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:01.13,1:18:02.49,Default,,0,0,0,,没问题吧？\NOK?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:03.55,1:18:12.88,Default,,0,0,0,,最终我们得到的是高斯分布和高斯分布之间的KL散度\NSo, what we end up with is a KL divergence of a Gaussian with a Gaussian.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:14.56,1:18:19.79,Default,,0,0,0,,我不确定你们是否记得 但我在这节课一开始时就说过\NAnd I'm not sure if you remember, but early in the lecture, I told you that
Dialogue: 0,1:18:19.79,1:18:23.56,Default,,0,0,0,,我们知道高斯分布的概率密度函数\Nwe know the probability density function of a Gaussian. We know.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:23.56,1:18:28.64,Default,,0,0,0,,我们能明确写出高斯分布的表达式\NWe have the explicit formula. We do know.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:28.64,1:18:36.13,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你把高斯分布的表达式代入KL散度公式\NSo, if you replace these into the KL divergence formula,
Dialogue: 0,1:18:36.13,1:18:40.57,Default,,0,0,0,,也就是代入到log(p/q)·p的积分里\Nwhich is this integral of log(p/q)p,
Dialogue: 0,1:18:41.79,1:18:49.20,Default,,0,0,0,,你会发现很多项都可以化简\Nthen, it turns out you have a lot of things that simplify.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:49.20,1:18:54.57,Default,,0,0,0,,最后你得到的就是\NAnd at the end of the day, what you end up with is
Dialogue: 0,1:18:54.57,1:19:01.31,Default,,0,0,0,,你想要预测的噪声\Njust the distance between the noise that you want to predict,
Dialogue: 0,1:19:01.31,1:19:07.20,Default,,0,0,0,,和你从清晰图像到带噪图像采样的噪声之间的距离\Nand the noise that you sample to go from the clean image to the noised image.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:07.20,1:19:09.59,Default,,0,0,0,,取它们的L_2距离\NTake the L_2 distance of that.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:13.11,1:19:15.71,Default,,0,0,0,,有关这个过渡过程 大家都清楚了吗？\NIs everyone clear with that transition?
Dialogue: 0,1:19:15.71,1:19:23.29,Default,,0,0,0,,我们所做的是 我们得到了ELBO 它等于这个KL散度项\NSo, what we did was, we had that ELBO, which was equal to this KL divergence term.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:23.29,1:19:30.20,Default,,0,0,0,,我们说 这看起来不错 因为我们想要计算的就是p_θ\NAnd what we said was, OK, looks good, because p_θ is what we want to compute,
Dialogue: 0,1:19:30.20,1:19:35.64,Default,,0,0,0,,然后 这个q是我们自己定义的 我们试着看看q是否是可处理的\Nand then, this q thing is something we have defined, so, let's try to see if it's tractable.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:37.68,1:19:44.23,Default,,0,0,0,,于是我们说 让我们看看q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0)是否是可处理的\NAnd what we said was, OK, let's see if q is tractable, q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0).
Dialogue: 0,1:19:44.23,1:19:48.12,Default,,0,0,0,,我们进入了数学推导 我们应用Bayes规则\NSo, we went into the math. We did the Bayes' rule.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:49.35,1:19:52.63,Default,,0,0,0,,我们通过后面的推导\NAnd then, there is this latter derivation around
Dialogue: 0,1:19:52.63,1:19:56.43,Default,,0,0,0,,确定了正态分布的均值和方差\Nactually, determining the mean and the variance of that normal distribution
Dialogue: 0,1:19:56.43,1:19:59.84,Default,,0,0,0,,我没有具体展开 因为内容太多了\Nthat I've not covered, just because it's just too much.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:59.84,1:20:03.17,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你在家自己推 结果就是\NAnd it's OK to just assume that if you do this at home,
Dialogue: 0,1:20:03.17,1:20:07.97,Default,,0,0,0,,一个具有此均值的正态分布\Nyou end up with a normal distribution of this mean.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:10.61,1:20:16.84,Default,,0,0,0,,我们也证明了p_θ是可处理的\NAnd then, we also showed that p_θ is something that is tractable.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:16.84,1:20:20.64,Default,,0,0,0,,方法就是假设p_θ是高斯分布\NAnd the way we have shown that is just by assuming that it is a Gaussian.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:22.19,1:20:25.67,Default,,0,0,0,,假设p_θ是具有某个均值和方差的高斯分布\NSo, Gaussian of some mean and then some variance.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:27.35,1:20:29.60,Default,,0,0,0,,最后\NAnd at the end of the day,
Dialogue: 0,1:20:29.60,1:20:37.92,Default,,0,0,0,,我们得到的损失函数就是对噪声的L_2回归\Nwe end up with a loss that is nothing else than an L_2 regression on the noise
Dialogue: 0,1:20:37.92,1:20:41.68,Default,,0,0,0,,即加到清晰图像上以得到带噪图像的噪声的L_2回归\Nthat we have added to our clean image to obtain the noisy image.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:44.71,1:20:49.69,Default,,0,0,0,,大家都同意这个损失函数看起来很不错吧？\NDo you agree that that loss is looking pretty good?
Dialogue: 0,1:20:51.33,1:20:53.64,Default,,0,0,0,,对吧？这个损失函数是可处理的\NYeah? It's very tractable.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:53.64,1:20:56.41,Default,,0,0,0,,你只需要回归你的噪声\NYou just have to regress your noise
Dialogue: 0,1:20:56.41,1:21:03.84,Default,,0,0,0,,以从清晰图像到带噪图像所加的噪声为目标 作为训练的损失函数\Non the noise from the clean image to the noisy image as a training loss.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:03.84,1:21:05.37,Default,,0,0,0,,损失函数很棒\NIt's great.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:05.37,1:21:08.40,Default,,0,0,0,,好了 我想...\NSo, OK, I want...
Dialogue: 0,1:21:08.40,1:21:09.31,Default,,0,0,0,,请问？\NYeah?
Dialogue: 0,1:21:11.87,1:21:13.31,Default,,0,0,0,,哦对 谢谢你\NOh, yeah. Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:13.31,1:21:15.49,Default,,0,0,0,,他的问题是 ε_θ是什么\NSo, the question is, what is ε_θ.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:15.49,1:21:18.08,Default,,0,0,0,,让我逐项解释\NSo, I'm going to go through each term.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:18.08,1:21:25.09,Default,,0,0,0,,幻灯片上给出的是DDPM的损失函数\NSo here, what is shown on the slide is loss of DDPM.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:25.09,1:21:28.00,Default,,0,0,0,,DDPM就是这整个框架\NSo, DDPM is this whole framework of
Dialogue: 0,1:21:28.00,1:21:34.55,Default,,0,0,0,,定义前向过程 然后确定如何反转过程\Ndefining a forward process in order to determine how you want to reverse the process,
Dialogue: 0,1:21:34.55,1:21:36.67,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是为什么损失函数叫L_DDPM\Nwhich is why it's called L_DDPM.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:37.88,1:21:43.31,Default,,0,0,0,,等号右边是\NAnd what is on the right-hand side of the equal sign is
Dialogue: 0,1:21:43.31,1:21:51.12,Default,,0,0,0,,对t取期望 t是你采样的噪声水平\Nan expectation over t that you sample, which is the noise level if you want,
Dialogue: 0,1:21:52.76,1:21:57.48,Default,,0,0,0,,x_0是训练集中的清晰图像\Nx_0, which is clean images in your training set,
Dialogue: 0,1:21:58.60,1:22:07.41,Default,,0,0,0,,ε是依标准正态分布采样的随机噪声\Nand then, ε is random noise that you sample from a standard normal distribution,
Dialogue: 0,1:22:07.41,1:22:14.33,Default,,0,0,0,,标准高斯分布就是均值为0、方差为单位矩阵的高斯分布\Nwhich is basically a Gaussian of mean 0 and variance the identity matrix.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:14.33,1:22:21.77,Default,,0,0,0,,期望里面的值 左边是ε_θ\NSo, what is in the expectation is on the one side, ε_θ,
Dialogue: 0,1:22:21.77,1:22:27.37,Default,,0,0,0,,这是你的模型预测出添加的噪声是多少\Nwhich is your model predicting what noise was added,
Dialogue: 0,1:22:28.52,1:22:33.24,Default,,0,0,0,,右边是ε 这是从清晰图像直接得到带噪图像时\Nand then, on the right side is ε, which is the actual noise that you added
Dialogue: 0,1:22:33.24,1:22:37.73,Default,,0,0,0,,你实际所增加的噪声是多少\Nfrom the clean image directly to the noisy image.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:39.71,1:22:41.33,Default,,0,0,0,,小括号里面的是什么？\NAnd what is in the parentheses?
Dialogue: 0,1:22:41.33,1:22:53.32,Default,,0,0,0,,√(ᾱ_t)x_0+√(1-ᾱ_t)ε 这等于x_t\NSo, √(ᾱ_t)x_0+√(1-ᾱ_t)ε, this is equal to x_t.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:53.32,1:23:01.56,Default,,0,0,0,,也就是带噪图像 因为你可以用清晰图像和ε\NSo, it's the noisy image, because you can go from the clean image and ε
Dialogue: 0,1:23:01.56,1:23:07.76,Default,,0,0,0,,通过我们之前的恒等式直接得到带噪图像\Ndirectly to the noisy image using the identity that we have seen.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:07.76,1:23:14.55,Default,,0,0,0,,换句话说 如果我给你带噪图像\NSo, in other words, it is saying, if I give you the noisy image,
Dialogue: 0,1:23:14.55,1:23:18.23,Default,,0,0,0,,请计算被添加的噪声\Nplease compute the noise that was added,
Dialogue: 0,1:23:18.23,1:23:21.72,Default,,0,0,0,,然后与实际添加的噪声进行比较\Nand compare that to the actual noise that was added.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:21.72,1:23:26.65,Default,,0,0,0,,我要指出的一点是 模型实际上有两个输入\NSo, one thing that I will call out is there are actually two arguments.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:26.65,1:23:30.81,Default,,0,0,0,,你不仅给模型提供了带噪图像\NYou not only give the model the noisy image,
Dialogue: 0,1:23:30.81,1:23:36.44,Default,,0,0,0,,你还告诉了模型表示噪声程度的信息t\Nbut you're also giving it the information of how noisy it is, t.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:37.95,1:23:41.45,Default,,0,0,0,,这里t在0到T之间\NSo here, t is between 0 and T.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:41.45,1:23:46.55,Default,,0,0,0,,如果t更接近0 说明没加多少噪声\NSo, if t is more towards 0, it means you didn't add a lot of noise.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:46.55,1:23:52.45,Default,,0,0,0,,如果t更接近T 说明加了更多噪声\NAnd if t is more towards T, it means you've added much more noise.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:53.69,1:23:58.17,Default,,0,0,0,,它让模型知道给定这张带噪图像 它带了多少噪声\NSo, it just allows the model to know, OK, given this noisy image, how noisy it is.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:58.17,1:24:02.71,Default,,0,0,0,,模型就可以校准要预测和去除多少噪声\NSo, it can calibrate how much noise to predict, to remove.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:04.59,1:24:07.01,Default,,0,0,0,,这样是不是清楚一些了？\NDoes that make a bit more sense?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:07.01,1:24:08.80,Default,,0,0,0,,好的 很好的问题\NPerfect, so, yeah, but great question.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:08.80,1:24:11.84,Default,,0,0,0,,我们接下来会\NAnd we're actually going to
Dialogue: 0,1:24:11.84,1:24:16.09,Default,,0,0,0,,精确地看看在实践中训练模型时这意味着什么\Ngo through exactly what that means in practice if we want to train the model.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:17.27,1:24:22.28,Default,,0,0,0,,但在此之前 关于损失函数 还有其他问题吗？\NBut before we do that, any other questions on the loss?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:23.40,1:24:24.24,Default,,0,0,0,,请问？\NYeah?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:26.93,1:24:29.65,Default,,0,0,0,,他的问题是 这个损失函数代表的是ELBO吗？\NSo, the question is, this loss represents the ELBO?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:29.65,1:24:34.01,Default,,0,0,0,,我们将在接下来的幻灯片中精确地看到\NSo, we are actually going to see exactly
Dialogue: 0,1:24:34.01,1:24:38.47,Default,,0,0,0,,我们是如何从第一步走到这一步的\Nhow we went from the first step to this step in the next slide.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:38.47,1:24:40.52,Default,,0,0,0,,我接下来讲的内容就可以回答你这个问题\NSo, I'm going to answer the question right now.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:42.89,1:24:45.85,Default,,0,0,0,,除了这个 还有其他关于损失函数的问题吗？\NSo, apart from this, any other questions on this?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:47.64,1:24:48.71,Default,,0,0,0,,没有其他问题了？\NWe're good?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:48.71,1:24:50.32,Default,,0,0,0,,好 我现在来回答你的问题\NOK, so, I'm going to answer your question now.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:50.32,1:24:58.65,Default,,0,0,0,,你还记得我们之前的四步策略吗？\NSo, do you remember the strategy plan we had with these four steps?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:58.65,1:25:01.23,Default,,0,0,0,,我们从\NSo, we went from
Dialogue: 0,1:25:01.23,1:25:07.04,Default,,0,0,0,,最大似然估计问题出发\Nthis maximum likelihood estimation problem that we wanted to perform.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:07.04,1:25:10.24,Default,,0,0,0,,我们说有一个下界\NAnd we said we have a lower bound.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:10.24,1:25:12.53,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是ELBO的由来\NSo, that's where the ELBO comes.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:12.53,1:25:18.24,Default,,0,0,0,,从ELBO 也就是从我们关心的量的下界开始\NThen, from the ELBO, which is a lower bound of what we care about,
Dialogue: 0,1:25:18.24,1:25:22.41,Default,,0,0,0,,我们把各项展开\Nwhat we said was actually expand the terms.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:22.41,1:25:23.37,Default,,0,0,0,,然后我们发现\NAnd we were like,
Dialogue: 0,1:25:23.37,1:25:28.21,Default,,0,0,0,,ELBO实际上包含一个KL散度 KL散度里面是两个看似可处理的项\Nwe actually have a KL divergence between two things that seem tractable.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:29.80,1:25:34.24,Default,,0,0,0,,然后 我们看了看KL散度项\NAnd then what we said was, OK, so, let's look at that KL divergence term.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:34.24,1:25:36.04,Default,,0,0,0,,KL散度项有两个部分\NThere are two parts to it.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:36.04,1:25:45.09,Default,,0,0,0,,一个是q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0) 另一个是p_θ(x_\{t-1\}|x_t)\NOne is q(x_\{t-1\}|x_t,x_0). The other one is p_θ(x_\{t-1\}|x_t).
Dialogue: 0,1:25:45.09,1:25:49.87,Default,,0,0,0,,我们看到这两项是可处理的 它们都是高斯分布\NWe saw that these two terms were tractable. They were Gaussians.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:49.87,1:25:54.51,Default,,0,0,0,,我们知道这两个高斯分布的均值是什么\NAnd we knew what the mean of these two Gaussians were.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:54.51,1:25:58.40,Default,,0,0,0,,然后我们说 有两个高斯分布\NAnd then, what we said was we have two Gaussians.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:58.40,1:26:01.25,Default,,0,0,0,,我们知道它们的概率密度函数\NWe know their probability density functions.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:01.25,1:26:04.45,Default,,0,0,0,,我们能得到它们之间的KL散度\NWe have a KL divergence of that.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:04.45,1:26:09.32,Default,,0,0,0,,我们可以计算这整个KL散度的解析解\NThen, we can actually compute this whole thing analytically,
Dialogue: 0,1:26:10.36,1:26:17.01,Default,,0,0,0,,最终结果就是一个非常简单的损失函数\Nand, as a result of that, end up with a loss that's very simple.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:17.01,1:26:21.45,Default,,0,0,0,,现在 有一个点我做了简化 但我没告诉你们\NNow, there is something that I simplified that I've not told you yet,
Dialogue: 0,1:26:21.45,1:26:23.69,Default,,0,0,0,,我现在讲一下简化的部分\Nbut I'm going to tell you now.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:23.69,1:26:29.33,Default,,0,0,0,,当你简化这个KL散度时 是实际得到的是\NWhen you simplify this KL divergence, what you actually get is
Dialogue: 0,1:26:29.33,1:26:35.88,Default,,0,0,0,,这个L_2回归的期望乘以一些系数\Nthe expectation of this L_2 regression times some coefficients.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:35.88,1:26:39.80,Default,,0,0,0,,你可以把这些系数理解为损失函数的权重\NYou can think of it as the weight of the loss.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:39.80,1:26:47.08,Default,,0,0,0,,训练模型的人可以选择是否引入这个权重\NAnd this is something that you as the person who's training the model can choose.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:47.08,1:26:51.60,Default,,0,0,0,,DDPM的作者尝试了不同的方式\NNow, the authors of DDPM, they try different ways.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:51.60,1:26:55.72,Default,,0,0,0,,他们试了真正的系数 也试了系数为1的版本\NThey tried the actual thing. They tried without by having a coefficient of 1.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:55.72,1:26:59.87,Default,,0,0,0,,他们发现效果也不差 因此可以让权重等于1\NAnd they actually said, OK, it's actually not that bad. You can actually take equal to 1.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:59.87,1:27:02.53,Default,,0,0,0,,但你确实可以自己选择使用其他的权重\NBut this is something that you can actually choose.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:03.91,1:27:08.32,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是你最终得到的这个表达式的过程\NAnd this is how you end up to this last expression.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:10.07,1:27:13.97,Default,,0,0,0,,来看看训练和推理\NSo, let's see how we do training and inference.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:15.29,1:27:17.64,Default,,0,0,0,,我们看一下策略 训练...\NSo, we see the strategy. So, training...
Dialogue: 0,1:27:17.64,1:27:21.43,Default,,0,0,0,,你要做的是最小化损失函数\NSo, what you want to do is to minimize the loss.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:24.24,1:27:27.35,Default,,0,0,0,,你的做法是 先采样...\NSo, what you do is you sample the amount...
Dialogue: 0,1:27:27.35,1:27:31.73,Default,,0,0,0,,首先 从训练集中采样一张清晰图像\NSo, first, the clean image from your training set.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:31.73,1:27:36.21,Default,,0,0,0,,采样噪声 然后采样时间步\NYou sample your noise, and then, the time step.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:36.21,1:27:39.71,Default,,0,0,0,,这样你就构造出了带噪图像\NAnd in that way, you constitute the noised image.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:39.71,1:27:44.25,Default,,0,0,0,,你可以对清晰图像加噪声得到带噪图像\NSo, you can go from clean image with the amount of noise up to the noised image.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:45.61,1:27:51.63,Default,,0,0,0,,把带噪图像和噪声水平输入给模型\NWhat you do is you take that noised image, you take the noise level,
Dialogue: 0,1:27:51.63,1:27:59.39,Default,,0,0,0,,用模型预测被添加的噪声\Nand then, what you do is you try to predict the noise that was added using your model,
Dialogue: 0,1:27:59.39,1:28:01.76,Default,,0,0,0,,我们现在还不知道模型参数是什么 模型现在就是一个黑盒\Nwhich right now we don't know. It's just a black box.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:03.09,1:28:06.00,Default,,0,0,0,,你计算损失函数 做反向传播\NAnd you compute the loss, and you do your back propagation.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:07.27,1:28:08.72,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是训练\NSo, that's the training.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:09.96,1:28:16.25,Default,,0,0,0,,推理过程是 采样一个噪声 这一步很容易\NAnd then, the inference is you sample your noise, which is super easy to do.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:17.79,1:28:19.64,Default,,0,0,0,,然后你要做的是\NAnd what you do is
Dialogue: 0,1:28:19.64,1:28:25.68,Default,,0,0,0,,一步步从噪声到更少噪声 再到更少噪声\Nyou go step by step, from noise to less noise, to less noise, to less noise,
Dialogue: 0,1:28:25.68,1:28:31.08,Default,,0,0,0,,直到到达t=0 也就是清晰图像\Nup until arriving at t=0, which is clean image.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:31.08,1:28:41.20,Default,,0,0,0,,这里 你所使用的表达式是p_θ(x_\{t-1\}|x_t)\NAnd here, what you do is you use the expression of p_θ(x_\{t-1\}|x_t),
Dialogue: 0,1:28:41.20,1:28:43.93,Default,,0,0,0,,我们已经推导过这个表达式\Nwhich is something we have derived,
Dialogue: 0,1:28:43.93,1:28:52.37,Default,,0,0,0,,这个表达式是一个函数 输入是带噪图像和预测出的去除噪声\Nwhich is a function of the noisy image, and the predicted noise that you can remove.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:53.51,1:28:55.44,Default,,0,0,0,,随后 你在上面再加一些噪声\NAnd then, you add some noise on top of it,
Dialogue: 0,1:28:55.44,1:29:04.40,Default,,0,0,0,,因为别忘了p_θ(x_\{t-1\}|x_t)是一个正态分布\Nbecause let's remember that p_θ(x_\{t-1\}|x_t) is a normal distribution.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:04.40,1:29:10.25,Default,,0,0,0,,这里加的噪声对应的是p_θ(x_\{t-1\}|x_t)的标准差部分\NSo, the noise here just corresponds to the standard deviation of that distribution.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:11.40,1:29:17.61,Default,,0,0,0,,当你从T一直走到0 你就得到了清晰图像\NAnd when you do that from T to 0, you then obtain your clean image.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:19.84,1:29:20.61,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NCool.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:20.61,1:29:24.11,Default,,0,0,0,,我知道内容很多 我知道这是第1节课\NI know this was a lot. I know this is Lecture 1.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:24.11,1:29:29.28,Default,,0,0,0,,这节课可能是8节课中最难的一节课\NI can tell you that this lecture is probably the most difficult of the 8 lectures.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:29.28,1:29:34.29,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你觉得信息量很大 这很正常\NSo, if you feel a little bit like it's a lot to digest, it's normal.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:34.29,1:29:37.75,Default,,0,0,0,,希望我们让扩散模型变得更容易消化了一些\NHopefully, we've tried to make it a bit more digestible.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:37.75,1:29:41.55,Default,,0,0,0,,幸运的是有录像 有笔记 什么都有\NLuckily, there is a recording. We have the notes, we have everything.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:41.55,1:29:44.17,Default,,0,0,0,,如果我们遗漏了什么 请告诉我们\NI mean, hopefully, if we don't, just let us know.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:44.17,1:29:46.65,Default,,0,0,0,,接下来 我把时间交给Shervine\NAnd with that, I'm going to give it to Shervine.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:49.80,1:29:51.47,Default,,0,0,0,,谢谢Afshine\NThank you, Afshine.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:51.47,1:29:57.00,Default,,0,0,0,,现在 我们看到了如何从噪声生成清晰图像\NSo now, we saw how to generate a clean image starting from noise.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:57.00,1:30:00.27,Default,,0,0,0,,在这个方程中我们看到\NAnd what we're seeing in this equation is that
Dialogue: 0,1:30:00.27,1:30:05.39,Default,,0,0,0,,需要重复同样的步骤T次\Nwe need to repeat the same procedure T times.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:05.39,1:30:14.21,Default,,0,0,0,,而这个T通常非常大\NAnd the thing is this T is usually quite large.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:14.21,1:30:18.65,Default,,0,0,0,,在原始论文中 T的量级大约是1,000\NSo, it's the order of magnitude of 1,000, for example, in the original paper.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:18.65,1:30:20.37,Default,,0,0,0,,假设\NAnd let's say,
Dialogue: 0,1:30:20.37,1:30:26.49,Default,,0,0,0,,你拿之前的图像生成模型作为参考\Nyou take the reference point of existing image generation models before that,
Dialogue: 0,1:30:26.49,1:30:28.23,Default,,0,0,0,,比如拿VAE或GAN作为参考\Nlet's say, VAEs or GANs,
Dialogue: 0,1:30:28.23,1:30:32.80,Default,,0,0,0,,你计算生成单张图像需要多少时间\Nand you compute the amount of time it takes to generate a single image,
Dialogue: 0,1:30:32.80,1:30:34.61,Default,,0,0,0,,之前的模型只涉及一次前向传播\Nwhich is the forward pass.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:34.61,1:30:37.23,Default,,0,0,0,,现在你要做T次前向传播\NSo, you have to do that now T times.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:37.23,1:30:40.09,Default,,0,0,0,,假设原来需要100毫秒\NLet's say you had to do it for 100 milliseconds.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:40.09,1:30:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,现在可能需要几分钟 这就不太好了\NNow, it might take the order of magnitude of minutes, which is not great.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:45.21,1:30:48.73,Default,,0,0,0,,从这里我们能得出的一个目标是\NSo, one comment that we have out of all of this is that
Dialogue: 0,1:30:48.73,1:30:52.92,Default,,0,0,0,,我们想在推理时降低计算负担\Nwe want to bring the computational burden down at inference time.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:54.67,1:30:58.27,Default,,0,0,0,,我们怎么做才能降低推理时的计算负担呢？\NSo, what can we do to make that happen?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:58.27,1:31:03.23,Default,,0,0,0,,我先展示Afshine之前展示过的方程\NSo, I will first show the equation that Afshine has shown,
Dialogue: 0,1:31:03.23,1:31:10.23,Default,,0,0,0,,这个方程关联了从步骤t到步骤t-1的生成过程\Nlinking the generation process from step t, which is a noisier image,
Dialogue: 0,1:31:10.23,1:31:14.29,Default,,0,0,0,,步骤t是噪声较多的图像 步骤t-1就是噪声较少的图像\Nto step t-1, which is the slightly cleaner image,
Dialogue: 0,1:31:14.29,1:31:18.72,Default,,0,0,0,,这个过程由幻灯片上的生成过程所定义\Nwhich was defined by that generation process written on the slides.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:19.96,1:31:25.25,Default,,0,0,0,,我们来试着让这些步骤变短\NAnd we're going to try to see how to make these steps shorter.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:27.52,1:31:29.71,Default,,0,0,0,,我们该怎么做？\NSo, what can we do?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:29.71,1:31:34.75,Default,,0,0,0,,一个策略是尝试跳过步骤\NOK, one strategy could be to try to skip steps.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:34.75,1:31:40.59,Default,,0,0,0,,我们首先想到的是写下方程\NAnd the first thought that comes to mind is to write down equations,
Dialogue: 0,1:31:40.59,1:31:46.17,Default,,0,0,0,,看能不能把一个低步骤和一个高步骤关联起来\Nand see if we can link a lower step to a higher one,
Dialogue: 0,1:31:46.17,1:31:48.71,Default,,0,0,0,,看能不能在两个步骤之间建立联系 从而跳过一些步骤\Nand see if we can make a connection between the two
Dialogue: 0,1:31:48.71,1:31:51.68,Default,,0,0,0,,而不需要经过每一个步骤\Nwithout going through each of the middle steps.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:51.68,1:32:00.03,Default,,0,0,0,,为此 我们先写出步骤t-1的方程 然后写出步骤t-2的方程 以此类推\NSo, let's start by writing down the same equation for step t-1, and then, t-2, and so on.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:00.03,1:32:07.19,Default,,0,0,0,,你会得到一个关联较低步骤和较高步骤的关系式\NAnd you come up with a relationship linking a lower step
Dialogue: 0,1:32:07.19,1:32:13.45,Default,,0,0,0,,这里我们使用另一个数列索引 我们就用τ_i好了\Nthat you index by some other sequence of numbers that you call τ_i,
Dialogue: 0,1:32:13.45,1:32:17.37,Default,,0,0,0,,τ_i是0到T之间的一个数列\Nwhich is a sequence of numbers between 0 and T,
Dialogue: 0,1:32:17.37,1:32:22.80,Default,,0,0,0,,相邻数字的间隔可能大于1\Nwhere the gap between consecutive numbers is bigger than 1, potentially.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:22.80,1:32:30.87,Default,,0,0,0,,最终你得到一个涉及步骤τ_i的关系\NAnd you end up with a relationship that involves step number τ_i,
Dialogue: 0,1:32:30.87,1:32:33.59,Default,,0,0,0,,其中τ_i是较大的步骤编号\Nwhich is the larger step number,
Dialogue: 0,1:32:33.59,1:32:41.45,Default,,0,0,0,,再加上一些数的求和以及一些采样噪声\Nand some sum over some numbers and some sampled noise.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:41.45,1:32:45.67,Default,,0,0,0,,但你会发现 这并没有带来多大进展\NAnd as you can see, it hasn't brought us very far,
Dialogue: 0,1:32:45.67,1:32:50.33,Default,,0,0,0,,因为你仍然需要做相当多次模型评估\Nbecause you still have quite a bit of model evaluations to make,
Dialogue: 0,1:32:50.33,1:32:53.47,Default,,0,0,0,,次数正好等于两个步骤之间的间隔\Nwhich is exactly the gap between the two steps.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:53.47,1:32:55.89,Default,,0,0,0,,这行不通\NSo, that didn't work.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:55.89,1:32:58.08,Default,,0,0,0,,我们接下来能做什么？\NWhat can we do next?
Dialogue: 0,1:32:58.08,1:33:01.67,Default,,0,0,0,,那我们就保留步骤数列τ_i\NSo, let's just keep that sequence of numbers
Dialogue: 0,1:33:01.67,1:33:08.45,Default,,0,0,0,,让τ_i表示跳过中间步骤的步骤序列\Nthat represents sequences of steps that skip some in between.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:09.97,1:33:16.48,Default,,0,0,0,,我们能做的一件事是尝试猜一个公式来关联不同步骤\NOne thing we could do is try to guess a formula that links two different steps.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:16.48,1:33:20.39,Default,,0,0,0,,我展示一个这样的公式\NAnd I'm showing you one proposal of such a formula.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:20.39,1:33:23.29,Default,,0,0,0,,我不打算推导它\NAnd I'm not going to derive it,
Dialogue: 0,1:33:23.29,1:33:28.11,Default,,0,0,0,,只是验证这个公式对两个连续步骤来说是成立的\Nbut just going to verify that this makes sense for two consecutive steps.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:28.11,1:33:36.24,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你让τ_i是步骤t 让τ_\{i-1\}是步骤t-1\NSo, if you say τ_i is step t, and τ_\{i-1\} is step t-1,
Dialogue: 0,1:33:36.24,1:33:39.08,Default,,0,0,0,,当你把数字代入\Nwhen you replace the numbers in there,
Dialogue: 0,1:33:39.08,1:33:44.60,Default,,0,0,0,,你会重新得到步骤t-1和t之间的关系\Nyou will find again the relationship between step t-1 and t.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:45.87,1:33:53.41,Default,,0,0,0,,假设你用这个关系来关联两个不同的步骤\NAnd so, let's suppose you use such a relationship to link two different steps.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:53.41,1:33:58.61,Default,,0,0,0,,你在实践中会发现\NThen, what you realize in practice is that
Dialogue: 0,1:33:58.61,1:34:05.63,Default,,0,0,0,,随着步骤中随机性的增加\Nas the amount of stochasticity that you have within steps increases,
Dialogue: 0,1:34:05.63,1:34:14.45,Default,,0,0,0,,你的图像生成质量将会随着步长的增加而下降\Nthen, your quality is going to get worse as a function of the step size.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:16.00,1:34:17.04,Default,,0,0,0,,大家能理解吗？\NSo, did that make sense?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:17.04,1:34:17.69,Default,,0,0,0,,顺便说一下\NSo, by the way,
Dialogue: 0,1:34:17.69,1:34:23.47,Default,,0,0,0,,这个部分的公式密度要比前面的部分略高\Nthe density of formulas in this last part is slightly higher than in the previous parts.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:23.47,1:34:27.68,Default,,0,0,0,,引入公式的目的是让大家更好地理解跳过步骤的直观思想\NAnd the goal here is more to get the intuition of skipping steps
Dialogue: 0,1:34:27.68,1:34:33.05,Default,,0,0,0,,我们要理解跳过步骤的运作原理 而不仅仅是单独地审视每个公式\Nand seeing how it works more than looking like at each formula separately.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:33.05,1:34:39.13,Default,,0,0,0,,到目前为止 大家都能理解吗？\NSo, yeah, so, does that make sense so far?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:43.56,1:34:44.85,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NOK, great.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:44.85,1:34:47.23,Default,,0,0,0,,现在 我们已经尝试了跳过步骤\NSo now, we have tried to skip steps,
Dialogue: 0,1:34:47.23,1:34:50.27,Default,,0,0,0,,并且我们找到了一个可以关联两个步骤的关系\Nand we have found a relationship that could link the two.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:50.27,1:34:55.43,Default,,0,0,0,,但我们看到步长太大时生成图像的质量不够好\NBut we see that the quality is not great when you take large step sizes.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:55.43,1:35:02.53,Default,,0,0,0,,因此 你要做的是尝试大步跳跃\NSo, what you're trying to do now is trying to do this large step skipping,
Dialogue: 0,1:35:02.53,1:35:07.96,Default,,0,0,0,,但避免步骤之间出现太多的随机性\Nbut avoid that level of stochasticity between steps.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:07.96,1:35:13.80,Default,,0,0,0,,为此我们回到原点\NSo, in order to do so, we go back to the drawing board,
Dialogue: 0,1:35:13.80,1:35:18.89,Default,,0,0,0,,看看DDPM的损失函数推导过程\Nand look at the derivation of the loss function that you had in the case of DDPM.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:18.89,1:35:22.11,Default,,0,0,0,,我们意识到的一点是\NAnd one thing we realize is that
Dialogue: 0,1:35:22.11,1:35:33.13,Default,,0,0,0,,让我们得到DDPM损失函数的关键部分是边际q(x_t|x_0)\Nthe key part to get to the formulation of the DDPM loss was the marginal q(x_t|x_0).
Dialogue: 0,1:35:33.13,1:35:34.97,Default,,0,0,0,,我们意识到\NAnd we realize that
Dialogue: 0,1:35:34.97,1:35:41.87,Default,,0,0,0,,当我们的建模选择能复现q上的这个关系时\Nwhen we do modeling choices that reproduces that relationship on q,
Dialogue: 0,1:35:41.87,1:35:50.12,Default,,0,0,0,,我们就可以得到一个基于相同损失函数的模型\Nthen, you can have a model that is based on the same loss.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:50.12,1:35:53.72,Default,,0,0,0,,这是第一个观察结果\NSo, this is one observation.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:55.25,1:36:00.44,Default,,0,0,0,,问题回归到找这样一个q\NSo, the problem statement comes back to finding such a q
Dialogue: 0,1:36:00.44,1:36:10.92,Default,,0,0,0,,使它复现这些边际概率 即边际概率仍然为q(x_t|x_0)\Nthat reproduces these marginal probabilities. So, with the same q(x_t|x_0).
Dialogue: 0,1:36:10.92,1:36:15.69,Default,,0,0,0,,第二个约束是\NAnd the second constraint that we want to put ourselves is
Dialogue: 0,1:36:15.69,1:36:21.45,Default,,0,0,0,,让生成过程去掉那个随机性项\Nto have a generation process that forgoes of that stochasticity term
Dialogue: 0,1:36:21.45,1:36:30.39,Default,,0,0,0,,看能否缓解步长增大时生成图像质量变差的问题\Nin order to try to see if we can mitigate the fact that quality of generation gets worse.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:31.68,1:36:33.80,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是问题陈述\NThis is the problem statement.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:33.80,1:36:37.83,Default,,0,0,0,,我用更数学的方式把问题写下来\NI'm going to write this down in more mathematical terms.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:37.83,1:36:44.39,Default,,0,0,0,,我们想找一个函数族 记作q_σ\NSo, we want to find a family of functions, let's say q_σ,
Dialogue: 0,1:36:44.39,1:36:47.65,Default,,0,0,0,,我一会就会介绍σ是什么\Nand I'm going to say what σ is very soon,
Dialogue: 0,1:36:47.65,1:36:51.68,Default,,0,0,0,,以及我们为什么讨论函数族\Nand motivates why we are talking about the family of functions here,
Dialogue: 0,1:36:51.68,1:37:00.65,Default,,0,0,0,,我们要求这个函数族与DDPM前向过程的边际分布相同\Nsuch that we match the marginals with respect to the DDPM forward process,
Dialogue: 0,1:37:00.65,1:37:03.91,Default,,0,0,0,,第二个条件就是我说的\Nand the second condition where I said that
Dialogue: 0,1:37:03.91,1:37:08.07,Default,,0,0,0,,我们不希望两个生成步骤之间有任何随机性\Nwe don't want any stochasticity between two generation steps
Dialogue: 0,1:37:08.07,1:37:10.20,Default,,0,0,0,,翻译成数学语言就是\Nis translated by the fact that
Dialogue: 0,1:37:10.20,1:37:16.97,Default,,0,0,0,,我们希望p_θ从噪声较多的图像到噪声较少的图像的过程是确定性的\Nwe want p_θ of the least noisy image given the noisy image to be deterministic,
Dialogue: 0,1:37:16.97,1:37:20.27,Default,,0,0,0,,这意味着一旦你有了x_t\Nmeaning that once you have x_t,
Dialogue: 0,1:37:20.27,1:37:25.89,Default,,0,0,0,,生成过程给你的x_\{t-1\}就是一对一映射\Nthen, your generation process gives you x_\{t-1\} as a one-to-one mapping.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:25.89,1:37:28.00,Default,,0,0,0,,不再有噪声项\NSo, there is no more noise term.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:29.76,1:37:32.32,Default,,0,0,0,,大家都同意吗？\NDoes everyone agree on that?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:35.09,1:37:41.92,Default,,0,0,0,,我来给你们一个公式 然后我来验证它满足这两个约束\NSo, I'm going to throw at you a formula, and verify that this works.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:43.13,1:37:52.07,Default,,0,0,0,,这个公式由一个叫σ的参数控制\NSo, this formula is parameterized by a parameter that is called σ here.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:52.07,1:37:54.96,Default,,0,0,0,,这个σ是一个超参数\NThat is a hyperparameter.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:54.96,1:38:00.71,Default,,0,0,0,,通过使用数学归纳法\NAnd by reasoning with the process of induction,
Dialogue: 0,1:38:00.71,1:38:02.56,Default,,0,0,0,,我们可以验证\Nwe can verify that
Dialogue: 0,1:38:02.56,1:38:10.64,Default,,0,0,0,,边际q_σ(x_t|x_0)和DDPM情况下的一样\Nthe marginals q_σ(x_t|x_0) matches the ones that we had in the case of DDPM.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:10.64,1:38:17.41,Default,,0,0,0,,且当你把σ设为0时 你可以看到\NAnd when you set σ to 0, you can see that
Dialogue: 0,1:38:17.41,1:38:23.77,Default,,0,0,0,,高斯分布就只有均值了 方差变成了0\Nthis term becomes just a mean with 0 variance.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:23.77,1:38:31.47,Default,,0,0,0,,你可以无随机性地关联x_\{t-1\}和x_t了\NSo, you can link x_\{t-1\} to x_t with no stochasticity.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:35.67,1:38:36.87,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NOK, great.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:36.87,1:38:39.73,Default,,0,0,0,,引入这样一个思路\NAnd so, this state of mind
Dialogue: 0,1:38:39.73,1:38:45.65,Default,,0,0,0,,以及意识到存在这样一个满足条件的函数族\Nand coming to the realization that you have such a family of functions that verify that,
Dialogue: 0,1:38:45.65,1:38:48.51,Default,,0,0,0,,并认识到探索此函数族很有吸引力\Nand the fact that this is attractive to seek
Dialogue: 0,1:38:48.51,1:38:51.24,Default,,0,0,0,,这些都是DDIM论文的一部分\Nis part of this DDIM paper,
Dialogue: 0,1:38:51.24,1:38:56.44,Default,,0,0,0,,论文标题相对DDPM唯一变化的就是\Nwhere the only term that changes with respect to the title of DDPM
Dialogue: 0,1:38:56.44,1:39:00.48,Default,,0,0,0,,P（概率性）变成了I（隐式）\Nis this P, probabilistic, to I, implicit.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:00.48,1:39:04.87,Default,,0,0,0,,DDPM中的概率性体现在\NSo, the probabilistic part of DDPM translated the facts that
Dialogue: 0,1:39:04.87,1:39:09.01,Default,,0,0,0,,当你从噪声生成清晰图像时\Nwhen you generated a clean image out of noise,
Dialogue: 0,1:39:09.01,1:39:14.51,Default,,0,0,0,,两个步骤之间有概率性\Nyou had this probabilistic nature between two steps.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:14.51,1:39:17.72,Default,,0,0,0,,但在DDIM的公式中\NBut in this DDIM formulation, where
Dialogue: 0,1:39:17.72,1:39:22.85,Default,,0,0,0,,两个连续的生成步骤之间没有随机性\Nyou don't have stochasticity at the generation step between two consecutive steps,
Dialogue: 0,1:39:22.85,1:39:31.05,Default,,0,0,0,,随机性只来自于你采样的初始噪声x_T\Nthe stochastic part only comes when you sample your initial noise, so, your x_T.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:31.05,1:39:35.92,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是为什么我们称扩散过程为隐式的\NAnd this is why we call the diffusion process implicit, because
Dialogue: 0,1:39:35.92,1:39:40.24,Default,,0,0,0,,因为在连续步骤之间没有概率性\Nthe probabilistic part is not something that you see between consecutive steps,
Dialogue: 0,1:39:40.24,1:39:44.60,Default,,0,0,0,,只有生成过程的最开始有概率性\Nbut rather sets at the beginning of the generation process.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:44.60,1:39:48.51,Default,,0,0,0,,我记得一开始有同学提的一个问题是\NSo, I think there was a question at the very beginning on
Dialogue: 0,1:39:48.51,1:39:52.05,Default,,0,0,0,,为什么不每次都从同一个点开始\Nwhy don't you start at the same point every time.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:52.05,1:39:57.72,Default,,0,0,0,,如果每次都从同一个点开始 那DDIM就不行了\NSo, if you were to do that, then DDIM wouldn't have worked,
Dialogue: 0,1:39:57.72,1:40:02.65,Default,,0,0,0,,因为一旦你设定了初始噪声点\Nbecause once you set your initial point of noise,
Dialogue: 0,1:40:02.65,1:40:06.15,Default,,0,0,0,,你就确定性地决定了最终图像是什么\Nthen, you determine deterministically your end image.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:09.09,1:40:13.27,Default,,0,0,0,,在这种情况下 我们能做的一件事是\NAnd then, in this case, one thing we can do is,
Dialogue: 0,1:40:13.27,1:40:21.60,Default,,0,0,0,,在每个步骤t都近似估计我们得到的清晰图像\Nat each step t, we can approximate our belief of what the clean image could look like.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:21.60,1:40:28.20,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你记得边际分布q(x_t|x_0)\NSo, if you remember, the marginal distribution q(x_t|x_0)
Dialogue: 0,1:40:28.20,1:40:33.01,Default,,0,0,0,,给出了x_t、x_0和噪声之间的关系\Ngives you a relationship between x_t, x_0, and the noise.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:33.01,1:40:40.67,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你重新整理各项 就可以让每个步骤都去近似x_0\NAnd if you rearrange the terms, then, you can approximate x_0 at every step.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:40.67,1:40:45.51,Default,,0,0,0,,把这几个项的顺序重新排列一下 你就能得到证明了\NThis is just the rearrangement of terms that proves that.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:46.72,1:40:52.83,Default,,0,0,0,,随后 你可以把x_0的近似值\NAnd then, you can plug-in that approximation of x_0
Dialogue: 0,1:40:52.83,1:40:55.71,Default,,0,0,0,,代入我们之前的公式\Ninto the formula that we had just before
Dialogue: 0,1:40:55.71,1:41:00.95,Default,,0,0,0,,通过适当加权来确定x_\{t-1\}\Nto determine x_\{t-1\} by weighting this term accordingly,
Dialogue: 0,1:41:00.95,1:41:09.21,Default,,0,0,0,,再加上步骤t-1所对应的适当权重系数的噪声\Nand adding to it adequate noise weighted by the right coefficient at step t-1.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:09.21,1:41:14.23,Default,,0,0,0,,可以注意到 这里没有额外的随机性\NAnd as you can notice here, there is no added stochasticity
Dialogue: 0,1:41:14.23,1:41:21.35,Default,,0,0,0,,这是由σ=0时q_σ前向过程族的构造保证的\Nby construction of this family of forward processes q_σ when σ=0,
Dialogue: 0,1:41:21.35,1:41:24.25,Default,,0,0,0,,这正是我们想要的性质\Nwhich is the property that we were after here.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:26.33,1:41:28.57,Default,,0,0,0,,到目前为止 大家都能理解吗？\NSo, does that make sense so far?
Dialogue: 0,1:41:33.72,1:41:34.81,Default,,0,0,0,,请问？\NYeah?
Dialogue: 0,1:41:36.87,1:41:39.17,Default,,0,0,0,,他的问题是 在哪里体现的跳步？\NSo, the question is, where's the skipping steps here?
Dialogue: 0,1:41:39.17,1:41:42.79,Default,,0,0,0,,到目前为止 我们都还没有跳步\NWe have not skipped any steps so far, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:42.79,1:41:46.13,Default,,0,0,0,,我们只是在构建生成过程\NWe're just constructing the generation process.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:49.99,1:41:51.28,Default,,0,0,0,,很好\NOK, great.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:51.28,1:41:54.27,Default,,0,0,0,,如果你回忆一下\NSo, if you recall,
Dialogue: 0,1:41:54.27,1:42:01.33,Default,,0,0,0,,DDPM的生成过程是不跳步的\Nyou had these DDPM generation process that you had that did not skip steps.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:01.33,1:42:04.84,Default,,0,0,0,,你必须一步步来\NSo, you had to go one step at a time.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:04.84,1:42:13.93,Default,,0,0,0,,现在 你可以把从步骤t到t-1的公式\NAnd now, you can adapt the formula that we saw from step t to step t-1,
Dialogue: 0,1:42:13.93,1:42:19.17,Default,,0,0,0,,改成步骤子序列τ_i的公式\Nbut now, between these schedules of steps τ_i's,
Dialogue: 0,1:42:19.17,1:42:24.17,Default,,0,0,0,,在步骤τ_\{i-1\}\Nwhere at step τ_\{i-1\},
Dialogue: 0,1:42:24.17,1:42:33.33,Default,,0,0,0,,你基于步骤τ_i预测对清晰图像x_0的最佳估计\Nyou predict your best guess at what the clean image x_0 is based on your step τ_i,
Dialogue: 0,1:42:33.33,1:42:37.21,Default,,0,0,0,,近似得到需要去除的噪声\Nand you approximate the noise that you need to remove.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:37.21,1:42:42.28,Default,,0,0,0,,你在步骤τ_\{i-1\}对每一项进行加权\NAnd you weigh each of these terms at the step τ_\{i-1\},
Dialogue: 0,1:42:42.28,1:42:45.75,Default,,0,0,0,,这样你就得到了这个公式\Nwhich is how you get this formula.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:45.75,1:42:48.73,Default,,0,0,0,,这里 我们定义了一些概念\NAnd here, we define some concepts.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:48.73,1:42:54.80,Default,,0,0,0,,当我谈到步骤序列τ_i时\NSo, when I talked about the sequence of steps τ_i's,
Dialogue: 0,1:42:54.80,1:43:04.13,Default,,0,0,0,,序列τ_i的总长度是S\Nso, the length of that sequence is S. So, we call it S.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:04.13,1:43:08.52,Default,,0,0,0,,T/S是有效加速比\NAnd T/S is the effective speedup.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:08.52,1:43:14.28,Default,,0,0,0,,我们不再需要花费T个步骤来生成一个新的样本了 花费S个步骤就够了\NSo instead of spending T steps to generate a new sample, you spend S steps.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:15.43,1:43:17.41,Default,,0,0,0,,考虑到这一点\NAnd with that in mind,
Dialogue: 0,1:43:18.68,1:43:26.15,Default,,0,0,0,,人们通常把加速比值设在10到100之间\Nthe value for the speedup that people typically take is between 10 to 100.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:26.15,1:43:31.15,Default,,0,0,0,,你应该能猜到 提高性能是要付出一定代价的\NAnd as you can guess, it doesn't come for free.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:31.15,1:43:36.07,Default,,0,0,0,,我们需要在生成速度和最终生成图像质量之间进行权衡\NSo, it's a trade-off between speed and actual quality that you get in the end.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:36.07,1:43:42.80,Default,,0,0,0,,人们实际采用的加速比值大致在10到50这个量级\NAnd the actual values that people take are more on the order of magnitude of 10 to 50.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:43.99,1:43:49.60,Default,,0,0,0,,这里展示了作者在一个实验中的结果\NAnd here, I'm showing what the authors showed in one of their experiments,
Dialogue: 0,1:43:49.60,1:43:52.68,Default,,0,0,0,,这里给出的是一个指标的变化趋势\Nthe evolution of one metric.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:52.68,1:43:56.72,Default,,0,0,0,,这个指标叫FID 即Fréchet Inception距离\NSo here, FID means Fréchet Inception Distance,
Dialogue: 0,1:43:56.72,1:44:01.45,Default,,0,0,0,,我们在第7节课讲评估时会介绍这个指标\Nwhich is a metric that we'll cover in Lecture 7 when we'll talk about evaluations.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:01.45,1:44:04.12,Default,,0,0,0,,现在我不会详细介绍这个指标\NSo now, I'm not going to cover it in detail,
Dialogue: 0,1:44:04.12,1:44:10.55,Default,,0,0,0,,只告诉你们这个指标反映了生成图像的质量\Njust going to tell you that it translates how the generated images look like.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:10.55,1:44:14.63,Default,,0,0,0,,FID的绝对数值本身没有太大的意义\NAnd so, the absolute values don't necessarily mean much.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:14.63,1:44:21.71,Default,,0,0,0,,但我们可以通过观察FID的相对差异来看跳步对质量的影响\NBut we can see the impact on quality based on relative differences.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:21.71,1:44:23.08,Default,,0,0,0,,你可以看到\NAnd you can see that
Dialogue: 0,1:44:23.08,1:44:29.04,Default,,0,0,0,,当把S的大小设置为加速比约等于20倍时\Nyou can speed up the process by taking S of size such that at that 20x,
Dialogue: 0,1:44:29.04,1:44:34.19,Default,,0,0,0,,图像生成质量与不跳步的基线相比差距并不大\Nyou're not too far from the baseline of not skipping steps at all.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:37.65,1:44:44.12,Default,,0,0,0,,这里我们讨论的是...\NYeah, so, the discussion here is...
Dialogue: 0,1:44:44.12,1:44:49.31,Default,,0,0,0,,我们意识到当跳步时\NSo, we realized that when you skipped steps, the stochasticity
Dialogue: 0,1:44:49.31,1:44:53.48,Default,,0,0,0,,两个连续生成步骤之间的随机性\Nthat you had between two consecutive steps that the generation process
Dialogue: 0,1:44:53.48,1:45:00.43,Default,,0,0,0,,会导致更低步骤的估计结果变差\Nturned out to generate worse estimates of what a lower step would be,
Dialogue: 0,1:45:00.43,1:45:03.87,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是为什么去掉随机性会更好\Nwhich is why removing it is better here.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:03.87,1:45:04.79,Default,,0,0,0,,这里\NSo here,
Dialogue: 0,1:45:04.79,1:45:10.75,Default,,0,0,0,,我们没有展示与不去除随机性方法的对比\Nwe don't show the comparison with methods that do not remove the stochasticity,
Dialogue: 0,1:45:10.75,1:45:13.09,Default,,0,0,0,,但论文详细展示了\Nbut the paper goes at length into showing that
Dialogue: 0,1:45:13.09,1:45:16.67,Default,,0,0,0,,当生成过程有随机性时 生成结果会差得多\Nwhen you do have stochasticity, the results are much worse.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:19.00,1:45:23.69,Default,,0,0,0,,我来总结一下整个过程的思路\NSo, if I had to summarize the thought process that we went through,
Dialogue: 0,1:45:23.69,1:45:28.00,Default,,0,0,0,,我们查看了DDPM的损失函数\Nwe looked at the DDPM loss.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:28.00,1:45:36.12,Default,,0,0,0,,我们查看了损失函数的核心成分 即q(x_t|x_0)\NWe looked at the core ingredients of what got us there, which was q(x_t|x_0),
Dialogue: 0,1:45:36.12,1:45:41.65,Default,,0,0,0,,我们选了满足相同关系的q_σ\NWe chose q_σ that verified the same relationship.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:41.65,1:45:45.59,Default,,0,0,0,,我们让q_σ使得...\NAnd we made q_σ such that it could be made...
Dialogue: 0,1:45:45.99,1:45:50.44,Default,,0,0,0,,我们让生成过程p_θ变成确定性的\NSo, we could have a generation process p_θ that is deterministic.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:50.44,1:45:55.64,Default,,0,0,0,,我们把确定性生成过程称为DDIM 有了确定性生成过程后\NAnd once we had this deterministic generation process, so, we call it DDIM,
Dialogue: 0,1:45:55.64,1:45:57.29,Default,,0,0,0,,我们进行跳步\Nand then, we skip steps,
Dialogue: 0,1:45:57.29,1:46:06.11,Default,,0,0,0,,从一个需要经过T个步骤的生成过程\Nand we get the transition from a generation process that needs to go through T steps
Dialogue: 0,1:46:06.11,1:46:09.68,Default,,0,0,0,,过渡到只需要经过S个步骤的生成过程\Nto one that only needs to go through S steps,
Dialogue: 0,1:46:09.72,1:46:14.49,Default,,0,0,0,,这就是我们最终得到的结果\Nwhich is what we got in the end.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:14.49,1:46:20.15,Default,,0,0,0,,感谢大家的认真听讲 祝大家周末愉快\NAnd with that, thank you very much for your attention and have a great weekend.
